{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011mXo4tzbfqk8hDnXc4zg78","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\n2\t\n3\t### type Key\n4\t\n5\t```ts\n6\ttype Key = readonly [number, Pose, Ease?]\n7\t```\n8\t\n9\t`[frame, pose, easeToNextKey?]`\n10\t\n11\t\n12\t### type Pose\n13\t\n14\t```ts\n15\ttype Pose = Readonly<Record<string, Euler | JointPose>>\n16\t```\n17\t\n18\tJoint name → rotation (degrees) or full joint pose. Missing joints are at rest.\n19\t\n20\t\n21\t### interface RigSpec\n22\t\n23\tEverything the tools need to know about a rig beyond its hierarchy.\n24\t\n25\t- `joints: readonly string[]`: Joint names in hierarchy order (root first).\n26\t- `root: string`\n27\t- `mirror: Readonly<Record<string, string>>`: Left/right counterparts for mirroring.\n28\t- `soles: readonly string[]`: Mesh names that touch the ground (soles).\n29\t- `trace: readonly string[]`: Points to trace in contact sheets (joint or mesh names).\n30\t- `limits: Readonly<Record<string, JointLimit>>`: Human-plausible rotation ranges, degrees.\n31\t- `fps: number`: Frame rate of the authoring format.\n32\t- `legs?: LegRig`: Leg geometry, enabling foot IK and the gait generator.\n33\t- `spine?: { torso?: string; head?: string; cap?: string }`: Joints the runtime procedural layers turn (PoseLayers): the torso and head look where the character is going; `cap` is an optional springy joint (not animated by clips).\n34\t\n35\t\n36\t### interface GaitSpec\n37\t\n38\tProcedural locomotion cycles with planted feet. Instead of posing every frame, describe\n39\tthe gait (speed, cadence, stance, bounce, arm swing...) and the generator plants each\n40\tfoot on the ground, sliding it backwards at exactly `speed` while it is in stance, then\n41\tswings it forward on an arc — heel strike, roll, toe-off included. Tweak numbers,\n42\tre-run `npm run anim -- check Walk`, look at the sheet.\n43\t\n44\tPhase: the RIGHT heel strikes at frame 0, the left at frames / 2.\n45\t\n46\t- `name: string`\n47\t- `frames: number`: One full cycle (two steps), frames at 30 fps.\n48\t- `speed: number`: Ground speed the cycle is authored for (m/s at playback rate 1).\n49\t- `stance: number`: Fraction of the cycle each foot is on the ground. Walk ≈ 0.55–0.6, run ≈ 0.3.\n50\t- `hip: number`: Mean pelvis height offset from rest (m); negative bends the knees.\n51\t- `bob?: number`: Pelvis bounce amplitude (m), twice per cycle.\n52\t- `low?: number`: Cycle fraction at which the pelvis is lowest (default: walk just after contact, run mid-stance).\n53\t- `squash?: number`: Squash at the lowest point (e.g. 0.05 = 5 % shorter, wider).\n54\t- `lift?: number`: How high the lowest point of the swinging foot clears the floor at its peak (m).\n55\t- `liftPeak?: number`: Where in the swing (0..1) the foot is highest (default 0.4).\n56\t- `reach?: number`: Shift the whole stride forward (m).\n57\t- `swingReach?: number`: Extra forward throw of the swinging foot late in the swing, before it settles (m).\n58\t- `swingDelay?: number`: Swing timing: 0 = even, + = the foot hangs back then whips forward (running).\n59\t- `plant?: number`: 0..1: how much the swinging foot sweeps back to meet the ground at touchdown. At 1 it arrives moving backwards at exactly the ground speed (still, in the world), so the foot plants without sliding; at 0 it eases to a stop relative to the hi\n60\t- `heelStrike?: number`: Toes-up angle at heel strike (deg).\n61\t- `toeOff?: number`: Heel-raise angle at toe-off (deg).\n62\t- `roll?: [heel: number, toe: number]`: Fraction of stance spent rolling off the heel / onto the toes.\n63\t- `tiptoe?: number`: Walk on the balls of the feet: extra pitch through stance (deg), pivoting on the ball.\n64\t- `swingPitch?: number`: Extra toes-down droop mid-swing (deg).\n65\t- `dangle?: number`: How much the swinging foot hangs from the shin mid-swing (0..1, default 0.8).\n66\t- `lean?: number`: Torso lean forward (deg) and twist of the shoulders against the legs (deg).\n67\t- `twist?: number`\n68\t- `sway?: number`: Side-to-side torso roll (deg).\n69\t- `pelvisPitch?: number`: Pelvis pitch (deg): tips the whole body, legs are re-solved.\n70\t- `head?: number`: Head pitch (deg) and how much it counters the torso twist (0..1).\n71\t- `headSteady?: number`\n72\t- `arms?: { /** Swing amplitude (deg). */ swing: number; /** Base elbow bend (deg). */ elbow: number; /** Extra elbow bend when the arm is forward (deg). */ pump?: numbe…`\n73\t- `pose?: Pose`: Extra joints/overrides mixed into every frame (hands, hat...).\n74\t- `extra?: (u: number, pose: Record<string, Euler | JointPose>) => void`: Per-frame hook for anything else: receives the cycle phase 0..1.\n75\t- `step?: number`: Key spacing in frames (default 0.5 — IK is non-linear, keep it fine).\n76\t- `notes?: string`\n77\t\n78\t\n79\t### type Instrument\n80\t\n81\t```ts\n82\ttype Instrument = Omit<SoundDef, 'freq' | 'freqEnd' | 'sustain' | 'delay'>\n83\t```\n84\t\n85\tA track's instrument: a SoundDef without pitch or length (each note sets those).\n86\t\n87\t\n88\t### interface HudOptions\n89\t\n90\t- `color?: HudColor`: Default 'white'.\n91\t- `shadow?: HudColor | false`: 1-pixel drop shadow color, or false. Default 'ink'.\n92\t- `scale?: number`: Integer art-pixel scale (2 = double-size glyphs). Default 1.\n93\t- `anchor?: HudAnchor`: Default 'top-left': x/y are offsets from that screen corner/edge, in art pixels.\n94\t\n95\t\n96\t### type HudColor\n97\t\n98\t```ts\n99\ttype HudColor = PaletteColor | number\n100\t```\n101\t\n102\t\n103\t### type HudAnchor\n104\t\n105\t```ts\n106\ttype HudAnchor = 'top-left' | 'top' | 'top-right' | 'left' | 'center' | 'right' | 'bottom-left' | 'bottom' | 'bottom-right'\n107\t```\n108\t\n109\tWhere an element is attached on screen; it is also aligned that way (right-anchored text grows left).\n110\t\n111\t\n112\t### interface ParticlePreset\n113\t\n114\tA particle effect as data. Sizes are in art pixels (whole pixels, so particles stay crisp\n115\tsquares), colors are palette names stepped over each particle's life (no blending).\n116\t\n117\t- `count: Range`: Particles per burst.\n118\t- `life: Range`: Seconds each particle lives.\n119\t- `speed: Range`: Launch speed, world units / s.\n120\t- `direction?: Vec3`: Main launch direction (default straight up).\n121\t- `spread?: number`: Cone half-angle around `direction`, degrees (180 = every direction). Default 180.\n122\t- `flatten?: number`: Multiply vertical launch speed (0.2 = dust that hugs the ground). Default 1.\n123\t- `gravity?: number`: Downward acceleration, world units / s² (negative floats up). Default 0.\n124\t- `drag?: number`: Velocity damping per second (0 = none).\n125\t- `size: readonly [number, number]`: Size in art pixels at birth and at death (rounded to whole pixels).\n126\t- `colors: readonly PaletteColor[]`: Palette colors stepped through over the lifetime.\n127\t- `radius?: number`: Random spawn offset radius, world units.\n128\t- `max?: number`: Pool size (max alive at once). Default 256.\n129\t\n130\t\n131\t### interface BurstOptions\n132\t\n133\t- `count?: number`: Override the particle count.\n134\t- `direction?: Vec3`: Override the launch direction (e.g. opposite to a skid).\n135\t- `speed?: number`: Multiply launch speed.\n136\t- `scale?: number`: Multiply size.\n137\t- `colors?: readonly PaletteColor[]`: Override the colors for this burst.\n138\t\n139\t\n140\t### interface PlayOptions\n141\t\n142\t- `volume?: number`: 0..1 multiplier on the sound's own volume.\n143\t- `pitch?: number`: Pitch shift in semitones (playback rate), e.g. a rising combo.\n144\t- `pan?: number`: Stereo position -1 (left) .. 1 (right).\n145\t\n146\t\n147\t### interface VoiceSettings\n148\t\n149\t- `volume?: number`: 0..1 (default 1).\n150\t- `pan?: number`: Stereo position -1 (left) .. 1 (right).\n151\t- `muffle?: number`: 0 (clear) .. 1 (behind a thick wall, under water): a low-pass filter closing down.\n152\t- `pitch?: number`: Pitch shift in semitones.\n153\t\n154\t\n155\t### interface Voice\n156\t\n157\tA looping sound steered while it plays (`AudioManager.loop`): a hum, a fire, a waterfall.\n158\t\n159\t- `readonly name: string`\n160\t- `readonly settings: Readonly<Required<VoiceSettings>>`: The values last set (kept headless too, so games and tests can read them).\n161\t- `readonly sounding: boolean`: Really sounding: Web Audio running and the loop started.\n162\t- `readonly stopped: boolean`\n163\t- `set(s: VoiceSettings): void`: Change any of its settings; they glide over a few hundredths of a second (no clicks).\n164\t- `stop(): void`\n165\t\n166\t\n167\t### interface CameraKey\n168\t\n169\t- `at: number`: Time (s) the camera is exactly here.\n170\t- `position: V3`\n171\t- `target: V3`: The point it looks at.\n172\t- `fov?: number`: Vertical field of view (degrees); default the previous key's, or 50.\n173\t- `cut?: boolean`: Jump here instead of gliding from the key before (a cut to a new shot).\n174\t\n175\t\n176\t### interface CameraShot\n177\t\n178\t- `position: [number, number, number]`\n179\t- `target: [number, number, number]`\n180\t- `fov: number`\n181\t\n182\t\n183\t### interface TimelineLine\n184\t\n185\t- `at: number`\n186\t- `until: number`\n187\t- `text: string`\n188\t- `who?: string`: Who is speaking (shown before the text).\n189\t\n190\t\n191\t### interface Cue\n192\t\n193\t- `at: number`\n194\t- `name?: string`\n195\t- `run: () => void`\n196\t- `cosmetic?: boolean`: Cosmetic (a sound, a puff of dust): not run when the scene is skipped past it. Cues that change the world (a door left open, an item given) are run on skip so the world ends up the same either way.\n197\t\n198\t\n199\t### interface PrecipitationOptions\n200\t\n201\t- `kind: PrecipitationKind`\n202\t- `count: number`: Most drops at once (the instance count).\n203\t- `area?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Width, height and depth of the air the drops fall through, around the centre.\n204\t- `color?: number`: Drop colour (hex).\n205\t- `speed?: number`: Fall speed (m/s). Rain 16, snow 1.4.\n206\t\n207\t\n208\t### interface WaterOptions\n209\t\n210\t- `size: readonly [number, number]`: Width (x) and depth (z) of the surface, m.\n211\t- `at: readonly [number, number, number]`: Centre of the surface at rest.\n212\t- `segments?: readonly [number, number]`: Grid quads along x and z (default: one per ripple cell, or 4 per metre without ripples).\n213\t- `waves?: readonly Wave[]`\n214\t- `ripples?: RippleField | null`: A ripple field covering the same rectangle (its size and centre must match).\n215\t- `deep?: number`: Colours (hex): troughs, crests, foam.\n216\t- `shallow?: number`\n217\t- `foam?: number`\n218\t- `foamAt?: number`: Height above rest (m) where foam starts. Default: 75% of the waves' combined height (the tallest crests).\n219\t- `opacity?: number`: 1: opaque; less: see-through by a 4×4 ordered dither per art pixel.\n220\t\n221\t\n222\t### interface NavGridOptions\n223\t\n224\tNavigation on a grid: which cells can be walked, the shortest path between two points\n225\t(A*, 8-connected, no corner cutting, smoothed by line of sight), a flow field toward one\n226\ttarget (one Dijkstra fill, then any number of agents read a direction per cell for free),\n227\tand line-of-sight tests (vision cones, stealth). Pure and allocation-light; unit-tested.\n228\t\n229\t  const nav = NavGrid.fromRows(['#########', '#...#...#', '#.#...#.#', '#########'], { cell: 1, origin: [-4.5, 0, -2] });\n230\t  const path = nav.path([-3, 0, -1], [3, 0, -1]);       // world points, corners only\n231\t  nav.flowTo(hero.x, hero.z);                            // once when the target changes cell\n232\t  nav.flowDirection(x, z, out);…\n233\t\n234\t- `cell?: number`: Metres per cell. Default 1.\n235\t- `origin?: readonly [number, number, number]`: World x, z of the top-left cell's corner (column 0, row 0). Default: centred on the origin.\n236\t\n237\t\n238\t### interface ButtonEvent\n239\t\n240\tA pointer button pressed or let go (`Input.buttonEvents`): its key, and where the pointer was (normalised device coordinates).\n241\t\n242\t- `readonly code: string`\n243\t- `readonly down: boolean`\n244\t- `readonly x: number`\n245\t- `readonly y: number`\n246\t\n247\t\n248\t### class Physics\n249\t\n250\tRapier world with a fixed 60 Hz step and render interpolation.\n251\t\n252\tPhysics owns the truth; visuals follow. Bound Object3Ds are *interpolated* between\n253\tthe last two physics states for smooth motion. Pixel alignment is purely a camera /\n254\tpresentation concern and never touches bodies here.\n255\t\n256\t- `static create(gravity = -24): Promise<Physics>`: Loads Rapier's wasm on first use (a separate, streamed .wasm file), then builds a world.\n257\t- `world: RAPIER.World`: The Rapier world. A new one per level (`clear()`): read it from here, don't keep it across levels.\n258\t- `alpha: number`: Interpolation factor between the previous and current physics step, 0..1.\n259\t- `steps: number`\n260\t- `readonly fields: ForceFields`: Zones that push, pull or drag (wind, fans, wells, currents): dynamic bodies get them every step, `PlatformerCharacter` reads them (physics/forces.ts).\n261\t- `stepMs: number`: Milliseconds Rapier took for one step (smoothed): what a pile of bodies costs.\n262\t- `update(dt: number, fixedUpdate?: (dt: number) => void): void`: Advance the simulation by real elapsed time. `fixedUpdate` runs before each fixed step (apply forces, move kinematic characters there).\n263\t- `state(): PhysicsState`: The physics as data, between frames (`engine.snapshot()`): the fixed step's clock and the whole Rapier world, exact. Bodies and colliders keep their handles across `setState`: a game finds its own again with `world.getRigidBody(handl\n264\t- `setState(s: PhysicsState): void`: Back to `state()`: the world it saved replaces this one, bound meshes re-found by handle.\n265\t- `restoreState(s: PhysicsState): PhysicsRestore`: `setState`, undoable: the saved world is built first (nothing changes if that fails), then replaces this one; `undo()` puts everything back as it was, `commit()` frees the old world. A mesh bound to a body the\n266\t- `get time: number`: Seconds of physics simulated (fixed steps × 1/60): the clock movers run on.\n267\t- `onStep(f: () => void, o: { first?: boolean } = {}): () => void`: Run `f` after every fixed step, before bound meshes (`bind`) read their bodies. Listeners run in the order they were added (instanced bodies keep their last two poses, a ragdoll holds its join\n268\t- `addMover(body: KinematicBody, options: MoverOptions): Mover`: Drive a kinematic body (`RigidBodyDesc.kinematicPositionBased()`) along a path, spinning or swinging, as a pure function of its own clock (physics/movers.ts), which starts at 0 now: the same howe\n269\t- `conveyor(collider: RAPIER.Collider, velocity: readonly [number, number, number] | null): void`: Make a collider a conveyor belt moving at `velocity` (m/s, world axes): dynamic bodies touching it are dragged along, the character standing on it is carried.\n270\t- `beltVelocity(handle: number): readonly [number, number, number] | null`: A conveyor's velocity, by collider handle (null: not a belt).\n271\t- `explode(at: readonly [number, number, number] | Vector3, o: ExplosionOptions = {}): number`: Push every dynamic body near `at` away from it (physics/forces.ts). Returns how many.\n272\t- `bind(body: RAPIER.RigidBody, object: Object3D): void`: Make `object` follow `body` (interpolated).\n273\t- `unbind(object: Object3D): void`\n274\t- `addStaticBox(o: BoxOptions): RAPIER.Collider`\n275\t- `addStaticCylinder(position: [number, number, number], halfHeight: number, radius: number): RAPIER.Collider`\n276\t- `addDynamicBox(o: BoxOptions): RAPIER.RigidBody`\n277\t- `tag(collider: RAPIER.Collider, ...tags: string[]): RAPIER.Collider`: Tag a collider with gameplay semantics the character controller understands: 'climbable' (ladders/vines), 'pushable', 'grabbable', 'slippery', 'noLedge', 'character', 'noCamera' (camera ra\n278\t- `hasTag(collider: RAPIER.Collider | null | undefined, tag: string): boolean`\n279\t- `raycast(from: Vector3, dir: Vector3, maxDistance: number, ignoreTags: readonly string[] = NO_TAGS): number | null`: Distance along `dir` (unit) from `from` to the first collider not carrying any of `ignoreTags`.\n280\t- `castRay(from: Vector3, dir: Vector3, maxDistance: number, ignoreTags: readonly string[] = NO_TAGS, exclude?: RAPIER.RigidBody): { distance: number; collider: RAPIER.Collider; normal: Vector3; point: Vector3 } | null`: Ray cast returning distance, hit collid\n281\t- `castUp(x: number, y: number, z: number, maxDistance: number, out: { y: number; nx: number; ny: number; nz: number; id: number }, ignoreTags: readonly string[] = NO_TAGS, exclude?: RAPIER.RigidBody): boolean`: Straight up from (x, y, z), at most `maxDistance\n282\t- `castDown(x: number, y: number, z: number, maxDistance: number, out: { y: number; nx: number; ny: number; nz: number; id: number }, ignoreTags: readonly string[] = NO_TAGS, exclude?: RAPIER.RigidBody): boolean`: Straight down from (x, y, z), at most `maxDist\n283\t- `groundBelow(origin: Vector3, maxDistance = 20, exclude?: RAPIER.RigidBody): { y: number; distance: number } | null`: Distance straight down from `origin` to the first collider (excluding `exclude`).\n284\t- `trigger(shape: TriggerShape, at: readonly [number, number, number] | Vector3, options: TriggerOptions = {}): Trigger`: A trigger volume with enter/exit callbacks (pickups, checkpoints, kill zones, doors). Checked after every fixed step against dynamic and k\n285\t- `updateTriggers(): void`: Run every trigger's overlap query now (Physics.update does this after each step).\n286\t- `isAlive(target: { isValid(): boolean }): boolean`: Whether `target` (a body, collider or joint) still exists in the current world: false once removed, and for anything from a level before (its world is gone; `isValid()` would throw).\n287\t- `remove(target: RAPIER.RigidBody | RAPIER.Collider): void`: Remove a rigid body (with its colliders and any bound Object3D binding) or a single collider. Removing a collider whose fixed body has no other colliders removes that body too (what `addStaticBox` &\n288\t- `clear(): void`: Empty the world: every body, collider, joint, character and vehicle controller, trigger, tag, binding, mover, field and belt goes; gravity and the solver's iterations go back to their defaults, the step accumulator and the step count reset. \n289\t- `fingerprint(): string`: A hash of the physics state: every body (position, rotation, velocities, asleep, enabled) and collider (pose, friction, restitution, sensor, enabled), exact, plus the step count and the time not yet stepped. Two runs that should be t\n290\t- `counts(): { bodies: number; colliders: number; joints: number; tags: number; bindings: number; triggers: number; controllers: number; vehicles: number; movers: number; fields: number; belts: number; }`: Sizes of everything Physics tracks (leak checks, debug\n291\t- `dispose(): void`\n292\t\n293\t\n294\t### interface RagdollOptions\n295\t\n296\t- `density?: number`: World density of the parts (the world's mass units per m³). Default 3.\n297\t- `damping?: number`: Linear and angular damping (air drag, joint friction). Defaults 0.1 and 1.5.\n298\t- `angularDamping?: number`\n299\t- `friction?: number`: Friction of the parts on the ground. Default 0.5.\n300\t\n301\t\n302\t### interface DecalOptions\n303\t\n304\t- `size?: number`: Width of the mark (m). Default 0.5.\n305\t- `rotation?: number`: Turn about the normal (radians). Default random.\n306\t- `color?: number`: Colour (hex). Default dark.\n307\t- `life?: number`: Seconds before it starts to fade (0: forever). Default 10.\n308\t\n309\t\n310\t### interface PlayerSettings\n311\t\n312\tThe player's settings: the standard picture and engine options every game gets, as plain data\n313\t(sound is the AudioManager's, which keeps its own volumes). A field left out is the game's own\n314\tchoice; a field set is the player's and wins over it. `engine.settings` holds them, applies\n315\tthem, saves them per game and shows them in the settings panel (the ⚙ button).\n316\t\n317\t- `look?: string`: A LOOK_PRESETS name. Left out: the look the game gives each level.\n318\t- `pixelArt?: boolean`: Pixel art (the pixel pass), or false for smooth 3D (render mode `raw`).\n319\t- `pixelSize?: 'fine' | 'chunky'`: The art resolution: `fine` (the game's, 480×270 by default) or `chunky` (two thirds of it: bigger pixels).\n320\t- `quality?: QualityOption`: Shadow and light quality: a level, or `auto` (the device's).\n321\t- `fps?: number`: Frame cap: 60, 30, or 0 for the display's own rate.\n322\t- `debugInfo?: boolean`: The debug panel: frame rate, camera, GPU errors and the game's status.\n323\t\n324\t\n325\t### interface Spatial\n326\t\n327\t- `gain: number`: 0..1 volume.\n328\t- `pan: number`: -1 (left) .. 1 (right).\n329\t- `distance: number`\n330\t\n331\t\n332\t### interface SpatialOptions\n333\t\n334\t- `ref?: number`: Within this distance (m) the sound is at full volume (default 1).\n335\t- `max?: number`: Silent from this distance on (default 30); it fades out over the last fifth.\n336\t- `rolloff?: number`: How fast it falls off past `ref` (default 1: inverse distance, the way sound really does).\n337\t\n338\t\n339\t### interface Listener\n340\t\n341\t- `position: V3Like`\n342\t- `right: V3Like`: The listener's right, in world space (unit): the camera's right for a third-person game.\n343\t\n344\t\n345\t### class ScreenFx\n346\t\n347\t- `cover(kind: TransitionKind = 'fade', o: TransitionOptions = {}): Promise<boolean>`: Cover the picture (progress → 1). Resolves when it stops: `true` when it is fully covered, `false` when another transition (or `set`, `clear`) took over first.\n348\t- `reveal(kind?: TransitionKind, o: TransitionOptions = {}): Promise<boolean>`: Uncover it (progress → 0) with `kind` (default: the one that covered it). Resolves like `cover`.\n349\t- `transition(kind: TransitionKind, between: () => unknown, o: TransitionOptions & { revealCenter?: TransitionOptions['center'] } = {}): Promise<boolean>`: Cover, run `between` (load a level, teleport), then reveal, also when `between` throws (the error is pas\n350\t- `set(kind: TransitionKind | null, progress: number): void`: Jump straight to a progress (0 clear, 1 covered), no animation.\n351\t- `flash(color: ScreenColor = 'white', o: FlashOptions = {}): void`: A full-screen flash that fades out.\n352\t- `shockwave(at: Vector3 | readonly [number, number], o: ShockwaveOptions = {}): void`: A ring that pushes the picture outwards from `at` (oldest ring is replaced when 4 run).\n353\t- `clear(): void`: Stop everything (a clear picture).\n354\t- `state(): ScreenFxState`\n355\t- `update(dt: number, camera: Camera | null): void`: Engine, every rendered frame (real seconds; `camera` projects world centres).\n356\t- `sampleNode(tex: any, scale: any): any`: Sample an art-resolution picture for the device pass, pushed by the shockwaves and blocked up by a mosaic transition, with the rings' bright edge. `tex` is the art target (a texture node); `scale` is device pixels per\n357\t- `colorNode(color: any, scale: any): any`: The transition and the flash over a finished colour (device pass).\n358\t\n359\t\n360\t### beltMaterial()\n361\t\n362\t```ts\n363\tfunction beltMaterial(base: number, stripe: number, o: { length: number; speed: number; pitch?: number; along?: 'u' | 'v' }): BeltMaterial\n364\t```\n365\t\n366\t\n367\t### hudSprite()\n368\t\n369\t```ts\n370\tfunction hudSprite(idOrDef: string | TextureDef, o: TextureOptions & { frame?: number } = {}): { rows: string[]; colors: Record<string, PaletteColor | number> }\n371\t```\n372\t\n373\tOne frame as `hud.sprite` rows and colours: a character per slot (a, b, c, … in palette order),\n374\t'.' for transparent.\n375\t\n376\t  const s = hudSprite('gem-icon'); hud.sprite(8, 8, s.rows, s.colors, { scale: 2 });\n377\t\n378\t\n379\t### buildModel()\n380\t\n381\t```ts\n382\tfunction buildModel(idOrDef: string | ModelDef, opts: ModelOptions = {}): ModelBuild\n383\t```\n384\t\n385\t\n386\t### interface ModelBuild\n387\t\n388\t- `readonly id: string`\n389\t- `readonly object: Group`: Named after the model; pivots are named Groups inside it.\n390\t- `readonly bounds: Bounds`\n391\t- `readonly anchors: Readonly<Record<string, { readonly at: Vec3; readonly rot: Vec3 }>>`\n392\t- `readonly colliders: readonly ColliderData[]`\n393\t- `readonly light: ModelLightRequest | null`\n394\t- `readonly report: ModelReport`\n395\t\n396\t\n397\t### addModelColliders()\n398\t\n399\t```ts\n400\tfunction addModelColliders(physics: Physics, build: Pick<ModelBuild, 'colliders'>, at: Vec3 = [0, 0, 0], yaw = 0): RAPIER.Collider[]\n401\t```\n402\t\n403\tStatic Rapier colliders for a placed model (its `colliders` data), at `at` turned `yaw`\n404\tradians about Y: a box, an upright cylinder or a convex hull, with `addStaticBox`'s friction.\n405\t\n406\t\n407\t### mergeStaticMeshes()\n408\t\n409\t```ts\n410\tfunction mergeStaticMeshes(sources: readonly Object3D[], options: MergeOptions = {}): Mesh[]\n411\t```\n412\t\n413\tMerge static meshes into one mesh per (material, shadow flags): N blocks with M\n414\tmaterials become ≤ M draw calls instead of N × groups (a BoxGeometry with 6 material\n415\tgroups is 6 draws, plus 6 more in the shadow pass).\n416\t\n417\tWorld transforms are baked into the vertices, multi-material geometry is split by its\n418\tgroups, and `position` + `normal` are kept, plus `uv` under a material with a `map` and\n419\t`color` under one with `vertexColors` (what toon materials read). The\n420\tsources are left untouched (don't add them to the scene). Physics is separate: keep\n421\tone collider per block. Merged meshes are culled as a whole, so merge things that are\n422\ton screen together (a level, a room), and keep anything that moves…\n423\t\n424\t\n425\t### interface MergeOptions\n426\t\n427\t- `castShadow?: boolean`: Override castShadow on every merged mesh (default: keep each source mesh's flag).\n428\t- `receiveShadow?: boolean`: Override receiveShadow on every merged mesh (default: keep each source mesh's flag).\n429\t\n430\t\n431\t### class Rng\n432\t\n433\tSeeded randomness. Everything random in a game comes from an `Rng`, so the same seed always\n434\tgives the same result (docs/DOCTRINE.md, principle 1). Each level gets one, `ctx.random`,\n435\tseeded from the engine's seed and the game's name; fork it by purpose so streams stay\n436\tindependent of how many numbers each one drew:\n437\t\n438\t  const level = ctx.random.fork(`level:${n}`);\n439\t  const room = level.fork(`room:${i}`);   // independent of how many numbers `level` drew\n440\t\n441\tNever use Math.random in game or engine code (the lint refuses it).\n442\t\n443\t- `new Rng(seed: number | string)`\n444\t- `get state: number`: The generator's whole state: save it, and set it back to draw the same numbers again.\n445\t- `next(): number`: Uniform in [0, 1). mulberry32.\n446\t- `fork(purpose: string | number): Rng`: A child generator for one purpose; does not advance this one.\n447\t- `range(min: number, max: number): number`: Float in [min, max).\n448\t- `int(min: number, max: number): number`: Integer in [min, max] (inclusive).\n449\t- `chance(p: number): boolean`\n450\t- `pick(items: readonly T[]): T`\n451\t- `weighted(items: readonly T[], weight: (item: T) => number): T`: Pick by weight; entries with weight <= 0 never come up.\n452\t- `shuffle(items: T[]): T[]`\n453\t- `gaussian(mean = 0, sd = 1): number`: Normal distribution (Box–Muller).\n454\t\n455\t\n456\t### class Hud\n457\t\n458\tPixel HUD: crisp text and icons drawn in art pixels on top of the game, never through\n459\tthe post filters. It is a 2D canvas at the internal resolution (480×270 / 320×180),\n460\tlaid over the game canvas with the same integer scale and letterbox offset\n461\t(`framing.ts`), so one HUD pixel is exactly one art pixel at every resolution.\n462\t\n463\tRetained: what you add stays on screen until `clear()`. Redraw everything each frame\n464\t(clear + add) or only when something changes; the canvas repaints only when the content,\n465\tresolution or framing changed. Available as `ctx.hud`.\n466\t\n467\t  ctx.hud.clear();\n468\t  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, `COINS ${n}/12`, { color: 'sand' });\n469\t  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, 'PAUSED', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2 });\n470\t\n471\t- `new Hud(container: HTMLElement | null)`\n472\t- `canvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null`: The overlay canvas (created on the first draw; null when nothing was ever drawn).\n473\t- `visible: boolean`\n474\t- `get width: number`: HUD width/height in art pixels (the internal resolution).\n475\t- `get height: number`\n476\t- `text(x: number, y: number, text: string, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: Text in the 5×7 bitmap font (uppercase; digits and common punctuation).\n477\t- `rect(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, color: HudColor, anchor: HudAnchor = 'top-left'): void`: A filled rectangle (panels, bars).\n478\t- `sprite(x: number, y: number, rows: readonly string[], colors: Record<string, HudColor>, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: A tiny pixel-art icon as data: one string per row, one character per pixel, mapped through `colors` ('.' or ' ' = transparent).\n479\t- `clear(): void`: Remove everything.\n480\t- `measure(text: string, scale = 1): { width: number; height: number }`: Size of `text` in art pixels at `scale`.\n481\t- `sync(resolution: Resolution, framing: Framing): void`: Engine: follow the renderer's resolution and framing, and repaint if needed.\n482\t- `dispose(): void`\n483\t\n484\t\n485\t### hudPlace()\n486\t\n487\t```ts\n488\tfunction hudPlace(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, anchor: HudAnchor, size: Resolution): [number, number]\n489\t```\n490\t\n491\tTop-left corner, in whole art pixels, of a w×h element placed at offset (x, y) from\n492\t`anchor` on a screen of `size` art pixels. Pure (unit-tested).\n493\t\n494\t{\"fps\":30,\"root\":\"Pelvis\",\"joints\":[\"Pelvis\",\"Torso\",\"Head\",\"ArmR\",\"ForearmR\",\"HandR\",\"ArmL\",\"ForearmL\",\"HandL\",\"LegR\",\"ShinR\",\"FootR\",\"LegL\",\"ShinL\",\"FootL\"],\"mirror\":{\"ArmR\":\"ArmL\",\"ArmL\":\"ArmR\",\"ForearmR\":\"ForearmL\",\"ForearmL\":\"ForearmR\",\"HandR\":\"HandL\",\"HandL\":\"HandR\",\"LegR\":\"LegL\",\"LegL\":\"LegR\",\"ShinR\":\"ShinL\",\"ShinL\":\"ShinR\",\"FootR\":\"FootL\",\"FootL\":\"FootR\"},\"soles\":[\"ShoeR\",\"ShoeL\"],\"trace\":[\"GloveR\",\"GloveL\",\"ShoeR\",\"ShoeL\",\"Head\"],\"limits\":{\"ShinR\":{\"x\":[-3,165]},\"ShinL\":{\"x\":[-3,165]},\"ForearmR\":{\"x\":[-160,5]},\"ForearmL\":{\"x\":[-160,5]},\"Head\":{\"x\":[-60,70],\"y\":[-95,95],\"z\":[-45,45]},\"FootR\":{\"x\":[-80,80]},\"FootL\":{\"x\":[-80,80]},\"HandR\":{\"x\":[-90,70]},\"HandL\":{\"x\":[-90,70]},\"Torso\":{\"x\":[-50,90],\"y\":[-70,70],\"z\":[-45,45]}},\"legs\":{\"R\":{\"upper\":\"LegR\",\"lower\":\"ShinR\",\"foot\":\"FootR\",\"hip\":[-0.14,0,0]},\"L\":{\"upper\":\"LegL\",\"lower\":\"ShinL\",\"foot\":\"FootL\",\"hip\":[0.14,0,0]},\"rootHeight\":0.62,\"upper\":0.3,\"lower\":0.22,\"ankle\":0.1,\"heel\":0.11,\"ball\":0.21,\"top\":0.02},\"spine\":{\"torso\":\"Torso\",\"head\":\"Head\",\"cap\":\"Cap\"}}\n495\tIdle:60L IdleLook:102L Teeter:30L Tiptoe:18L Walk:12L Run:12L Skid:18 SkidTurn:12 StepUp:8 StepDown:8 Crouch:40L CrouchWalk:12L CrouchSlide:20L ProneDown:16 Prone:60L Crawl:36L GetUpFront:21 Sit:60L SitDown:16 StandUp:16 LieDown:30 LieIdle:60L Sleep:90L GetUp:24 Jump:20 JumpUp:20 DoubleJump:22 TripleJump:30 Backflip:30 SideFlip:26 LongJump:36 WallKick:20 WallSlide:20L Fall:16L Dive:12 BellySlide:20L GroundPoundSpin:9 GroundPound:10 GroundPoundLand:15 Land:10 HardLand:30 Slide:20L Hang:40L ShimmyRight:20L ShimmyLeft:20L PullUp:27 ClimbIdle:40L Climb:24L Push:30L PushIdle:40L Grab:40L Pull:30L Punch:10 Punch2:10 Kick:14 SweepKick:18 JumpKick:14 Wave:44 Victory:48 Hurt:20 Slash1:12 Slash2:12 Slash3:18 Slam:24 LeapSlam:28 Spin:12L Cast:16 CastBig:22 CastWeapon:16 CastBigWeapon:22 BowDraw:18 BowRelease:12 Roll:14 Charge:14 Shout:20 HitReact:10 Death:36 Triumph:40\n496\t{\"name\":\"Kick\",\"fast\":true,\"frames\":14,\"grounded\":true,\"keys\":[[0,{\"Pelvis\":{\"r\":[0,0,0],\"p\":[0,-0.07,0],\"s\":1},\"Torso\":[8,0,0],\"Head\":[-6,0,0],\"ArmR\":[-40,0,-16],\"ForearmR\":[-115,0,0],\"HandR\":[-10,0,0],\"ArmL\":[-48,0,16],\"ForearmL\":[-120,0,0],\"HandL\":[-10,0,0],\"LegR\":{\"r\":[-7.388,0,0],\"p\":[0,0,0],\"s\":[1,1,1]},\"ShinR\":{\"r\":[53.509,0,0],\"p\":[0,0,0],\"s\":[1,1,1]},\"FootR\":{\"r\":[-46.121,0,0],\"p\":[0,0,0],\"s\":[1,1,1]},\"LegL\":{\"r\":[-38.441,0,0],\"p\":[0,0,0],\"s\":[1,1,1]},\"ShinL\":{\"r\":[50.647,0,0],\"p\":[0,0,0],\"s\":[1,1,1]},\"FootL\":{\"r\":[-12.206,0,0],\"p\":[0,0,0],\"s\":[1,1,1]}},null],[4,{\"Pelvis\":{\"r\":[0,0,0],\"p\":[0,-0.07,0],\"s\":1},\"Torso\":[-6,0,0],\"Head\":[-6,0,0],\"ArmR\":[-30,0,-50],\"ForearmR\":[-60,0,0],\"HandR\":[0,0,0],\"ArmL\":[-60,0,40],\"ForearmL\":[-60,0,0],\"HandL\":[0,0,0],\"LegR\":[-85,0,-5],\"ShinR\":[110,0,0],\"FootR\":[20,0,0],\"LegL\":{\"r\":[-38.441,0,0],\"p\":[0,0,0],\"s\":[1,1,1]},\"ShinL\":{\"r\":[50.647,0,0],\"p\n497\t[{\"bone\":\"Pelvis\",\"from\":[-0.12,-0.04,0],\"to\":[0.12,-0.04,0],\"radius\":0.13},{\"bone\":\"Torso\",\"parent\":\"Pelvis\",\"from\":[0,0.16,0],\"to\":[0,0.42,0],\"radius\":0.2,\"cone\":35},{\"bone\":\"Head\",\"parent\":\"Torso\",\"from\":[0,0.2,0],\"to\":[0,0.34,0],\"radius\":0.22,\"cone\":40,\"density\":0.7},{\"bone\":\"ArmR\",\"parent\":\"Torso\",\"to\":[0,-0.25,0],\"radius\":0.07,\"cone\":100},{\"bone\":\"ForearmR\",\"parent\":\"ArmR\",\"to\":[0,-0.26,0],\"radius\":0.07,\"hinge\":[-150,0]},{\"bone\":\"ArmL\",\"parent\":\"Torso\",\"to\":[0,-0.25,0],\"radius\":0.07,\"cone\"\n498\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76d12802-c986-437e-adae-1ae347966275","uuid":"8ff161c5-3c65-4f0f-9ce6-994d6b1963f5","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:21:59.975Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-medium-build-v2--20261105-162048--xa8053f-work/76d12802-c986-437e-adae-1ae347966275/tool-results/bigyxcfok.txt","content":"\n\n### type Key\n\n```ts\ntype Key = readonly [number, Pose, Ease?]\n```\n\n`[frame, pose, easeToNextKey?]`\n\n\n### type Pose\n\n```ts\ntype Pose = Readonly<Record<string, Euler | JointPose>>\n```\n\nJoint name → rotation (degrees) or full joint pose. Missing joints are at rest.\n\n\n### interface RigSpec\n\nEverything the tools need to know about a rig beyond its hierarchy.\n\n- `joints: readonly string[]`: Joint names in hierarchy order (root first).\n- `root: string`\n- `mirror: Readonly<Record<string, string>>`: Left/right counterparts for mirroring.\n- `soles: readonly string[]`: Mesh names that touch the ground (soles).\n- `trace: readonly string[]`: Points to trace in contact sheets (joint or mesh names).\n- `limits: Readonly<Record<string, JointLimit>>`: Human-plausible rotation ranges, degrees.\n- `fps: number`: Frame rate of the authoring format.\n- `legs?: LegRig`: Leg geometry, enabling foot IK and the gait generator.\n- `spine?: { torso?: string; head?: string; cap?: string }`: Joints the runtime procedural layers turn (PoseLayers): the torso and head look where the character is going; `cap` is an optional springy joint (not animated by clips).\n\n\n### interface GaitSpec\n\nProcedural locomotion cycles with planted feet. Instead of posing every frame, describe\nthe gait (speed, cadence, stance, bounce, arm swing...) and the generator plants each\nfoot on the ground, sliding it backwards at exactly `speed` while it is in stance, then\nswings it forward on an arc — heel strike, roll, toe-off included. Tweak numbers,\nre-run `npm run anim -- check Walk`, look at the sheet.\n\nPhase: the RIGHT heel strikes at frame 0, the left at frames / 2.\n\n- `name: string`\n- `frames: number`: One full cycle (two steps), frames at 30 fps.\n- `speed: number`: Ground speed the cycle is authored for (m/s at playback rate 1).\n- `stance: number`: Fraction of the cycle each foot is on the ground. Walk ≈ 0.55–0.6, run ≈ 0.3.\n- `hip: number`: Mean pelvis height offset from rest (m); negative bends the knees.\n- `bob?: number`: Pelvis bounce amplitude (m), twice per cycle.\n- `low?: number`: Cycle fraction at which the pelvis is lowest (default: walk just after contact, run mid-stance).\n- `squash?: number`: Squash at the lowest point (e.g. 0.05 = 5 % shorter, wider).\n- `lift?: number`: How high the lowest point of the swinging foot clears the floor at its peak (m).\n- `liftPeak?: number`: Where in the swing (0..1) the foot is highest (default 0.4).\n- `reach?: number`: Shift the whole stride forward (m).\n- `swingReach?: number`: Extra forward throw of the swinging foot late in the swing, before it settles (m).\n- `swingDelay?: number`: Swing timing: 0 = even, + = the foot hangs back then whips forward (running).\n- `plant?: number`: 0..1: how much the swinging foot sweeps back to meet the ground at touchdown. At 1 it arrives moving backwards at exactly the ground speed (still, in the world), so the foot plants without sliding; at 0 it eases to a stop relative to the hi\n- `heelStrike?: number`: Toes-up angle at heel strike (deg).\n- `toeOff?: number`: Heel-raise angle at toe-off (deg).\n- `roll?: [heel: number, toe: number]`: Fraction of stance spent rolling off the heel / onto the toes.\n- `tiptoe?: number`: Walk on the balls of the feet: extra pitch through stance (deg), pivoting on the ball.\n- `swingPitch?: number`: Extra toes-down droop mid-swing (deg).\n- `dangle?: number`: How much the swinging foot hangs from the shin mid-swing (0..1, default 0.8).\n- `lean?: number`: Torso lean forward (deg) and twist of the shoulders against the legs (deg).\n- `twist?: number`\n- `sway?: number`: Side-to-side torso roll (deg).\n- `pelvisPitch?: number`: Pelvis pitch (deg): tips the whole body, legs are re-solved.\n- `head?: number`: Head pitch (deg) and how much it counters the torso twist (0..1).\n- `headSteady?: number`\n- `arms?: { /** Swing amplitude (deg). */ swing: number; /** Base elbow bend (deg). */ elbow: number; /** Extra elbow bend when the arm is forward (deg). */ pump?: numbe…`\n- `pose?: Pose`: Extra joints/overrides mixed into every frame (hands, hat...).\n- `extra?: (u: number, pose: Record<string, Euler | JointPose>) => void`: Per-frame hook for anything else: receives the cycle phase 0..1.\n- `step?: number`: Key spacing in frames (default 0.5 — IK is non-linear, keep it fine).\n- `notes?: string`\n\n\n### type Instrument\n\n```ts\ntype Instrument = Omit<SoundDef, 'freq' | 'freqEnd' | 'sustain' | 'delay'>\n```\n\nA track's instrument: a SoundDef without pitch or length (each note sets those).\n\n\n### interface HudOptions\n\n- `color?: HudColor`: Default 'white'.\n- `shadow?: HudColor | false`: 1-pixel drop shadow color, or false. Default 'ink'.\n- `scale?: number`: Integer art-pixel scale (2 = double-size glyphs). Default 1.\n- `anchor?: HudAnchor`: Default 'top-left': x/y are offsets from that screen corner/edge, in art pixels.\n\n\n### type HudColor\n\n```ts\ntype HudColor = PaletteColor | number\n```\n\n\n### type HudAnchor\n\n```ts\ntype HudAnchor = 'top-left' | 'top' | 'top-right' | 'left' | 'center' | 'right' | 'bottom-left' | 'bottom' | 'bottom-right'\n```\n\nWhere an element is attached on screen; it is also aligned that way (right-anchored text grows left).\n\n\n### interface ParticlePreset\n\nA particle effect as data. Sizes are in art pixels (whole pixels, so particles stay crisp\nsquares), colors are palette names stepped over each particle's life (no blending).\n\n- `count: Range`: Particles per burst.\n- `life: Range`: Seconds each particle lives.\n- `speed: Range`: Launch speed, world units / s.\n- `direction?: Vec3`: Main launch direction (default straight up).\n- `spread?: number`: Cone half-angle around `direction`, degrees (180 = every direction). Default 180.\n- `flatten?: number`: Multiply vertical launch speed (0.2 = dust that hugs the ground). Default 1.\n- `gravity?: number`: Downward acceleration, world units / s² (negative floats up). Default 0.\n- `drag?: number`: Velocity damping per second (0 = none).\n- `size: readonly [number, number]`: Size in art pixels at birth and at death (rounded to whole pixels).\n- `colors: readonly PaletteColor[]`: Palette colors stepped through over the lifetime.\n- `radius?: number`: Random spawn offset radius, world units.\n- `max?: number`: Pool size (max alive at once). Default 256.\n\n\n### interface BurstOptions\n\n- `count?: number`: Override the particle count.\n- `direction?: Vec3`: Override the launch direction (e.g. opposite to a skid).\n- `speed?: number`: Multiply launch speed.\n- `scale?: number`: Multiply size.\n- `colors?: readonly PaletteColor[]`: Override the colors for this burst.\n\n\n### interface PlayOptions\n\n- `volume?: number`: 0..1 multiplier on the sound's own volume.\n- `pitch?: number`: Pitch shift in semitones (playback rate), e.g. a rising combo.\n- `pan?: number`: Stereo position -1 (left) .. 1 (right).\n\n\n### interface VoiceSettings\n\n- `volume?: number`: 0..1 (default 1).\n- `pan?: number`: Stereo position -1 (left) .. 1 (right).\n- `muffle?: number`: 0 (clear) .. 1 (behind a thick wall, under water): a low-pass filter closing down.\n- `pitch?: number`: Pitch shift in semitones.\n\n\n### interface Voice\n\nA looping sound steered while it plays (`AudioManager.loop`): a hum, a fire, a waterfall.\n\n- `readonly name: string`\n- `readonly settings: Readonly<Required<VoiceSettings>>`: The values last set (kept headless too, so games and tests can read them).\n- `readonly sounding: boolean`: Really sounding: Web Audio running and the loop started.\n- `readonly stopped: boolean`\n- `set(s: VoiceSettings): void`: Change any of its settings; they glide over a few hundredths of a second (no clicks).\n- `stop(): void`\n\n\n### interface CameraKey\n\n- `at: number`: Time (s) the camera is exactly here.\n- `position: V3`\n- `target: V3`: The point it looks at.\n- `fov?: number`: Vertical field of view (degrees); default the previous key's, or 50.\n- `cut?: boolean`: Jump here instead of gliding from the key before (a cut to a new shot).\n\n\n### interface CameraShot\n\n- `position: [number, number, number]`\n- `target: [number, number, number]`\n- `fov: number`\n\n\n### interface TimelineLine\n\n- `at: number`\n- `until: number`\n- `text: string`\n- `who?: string`: Who is speaking (shown before the text).\n\n\n### interface Cue\n\n- `at: number`\n- `name?: string`\n- `run: () => void`\n- `cosmetic?: boolean`: Cosmetic (a sound, a puff of dust): not run when the scene is skipped past it. Cues that change the world (a door left open, an item given) are run on skip so the world ends up the same either way.\n\n\n### interface PrecipitationOptions\n\n- `kind: PrecipitationKind`\n- `count: number`: Most drops at once (the instance count).\n- `area?: readonly [number, number, number]`: Width, height and depth of the air the drops fall through, around the centre.\n- `color?: number`: Drop colour (hex).\n- `speed?: number`: Fall speed (m/s). Rain 16, snow 1.4.\n\n\n### interface WaterOptions\n\n- `size: readonly [number, number]`: Width (x) and depth (z) of the surface, m.\n- `at: readonly [number, number, number]`: Centre of the surface at rest.\n- `segments?: readonly [number, number]`: Grid quads along x and z (default: one per ripple cell, or 4 per metre without ripples).\n- `waves?: readonly Wave[]`\n- `ripples?: RippleField | null`: A ripple field covering the same rectangle (its size and centre must match).\n- `deep?: number`: Colours (hex): troughs, crests, foam.\n- `shallow?: number`\n- `foam?: number`\n- `foamAt?: number`: Height above rest (m) where foam starts. Default: 75% of the waves' combined height (the tallest crests).\n- `opacity?: number`: 1: opaque; less: see-through by a 4×4 ordered dither per art pixel.\n\n\n### interface NavGridOptions\n\nNavigation on a grid: which cells can be walked, the shortest path between two points\n(A*, 8-connected, no corner cutting, smoothed by line of sight), a flow field toward one\ntarget (one Dijkstra fill, then any number of agents read a direction per cell for free),\nand line-of-sight tests (vision cones, stealth). Pure and allocation-light; unit-tested.\n\n  const nav = NavGrid.fromRows(['#########', '#...#...#', '#.#...#.#', '#########'], { cell: 1, origin: [-4.5, 0, -2] });\n  const path = nav.path([-3, 0, -1], [3, 0, -1]);       // world points, corners only\n  nav.flowTo(hero.x, hero.z);                            // once when the target changes cell\n  nav.flowDirection(x, z, out);…\n\n- `cell?: number`: Metres per cell. Default 1.\n- `origin?: readonly [number, number, number]`: World x, z of the top-left cell's corner (column 0, row 0). Default: centred on the origin.\n\n\n### interface ButtonEvent\n\nA pointer button pressed or let go (`Input.buttonEvents`): its key, and where the pointer was (normalised device coordinates).\n\n- `readonly code: string`\n- `readonly down: boolean`\n- `readonly x: number`\n- `readonly y: number`\n\n\n### class Physics\n\nRapier world with a fixed 60 Hz step and render interpolation.\n\nPhysics owns the truth; visuals follow. Bound Object3Ds are *interpolated* between\nthe last two physics states for smooth motion. Pixel alignment is purely a camera /\npresentation concern and never touches bodies here.\n\n- `static create(gravity = -24): Promise<Physics>`: Loads Rapier's wasm on first use (a separate, streamed .wasm file), then builds a world.\n- `world: RAPIER.World`: The Rapier world. A new one per level (`clear()`): read it from here, don't keep it across levels.\n- `alpha: number`: Interpolation factor between the previous and current physics step, 0..1.\n- `steps: number`\n- `readonly fields: ForceFields`: Zones that push, pull or drag (wind, fans, wells, currents): dynamic bodies get them every step, `PlatformerCharacter` reads them (physics/forces.ts).\n- `stepMs: number`: Milliseconds Rapier took for one step (smoothed): what a pile of bodies costs.\n- `update(dt: number, fixedUpdate?: (dt: number) => void): void`: Advance the simulation by real elapsed time. `fixedUpdate` runs before each fixed step (apply forces, move kinematic characters there).\n- `state(): PhysicsState`: The physics as data, between frames (`engine.snapshot()`): the fixed step's clock and the whole Rapier world, exact. Bodies and colliders keep their handles across `setState`: a game finds its own again with `world.getRigidBody(handl\n- `setState(s: PhysicsState): void`: Back to `state()`: the world it saved replaces this one, bound meshes re-found by handle.\n- `restoreState(s: PhysicsState): PhysicsRestore`: `setState`, undoable: the saved world is built first (nothing changes if that fails), then replaces this one; `undo()` puts everything back as it was, `commit()` frees the old world. A mesh bound to a body the\n- `get time: number`: Seconds of physics simulated (fixed steps × 1/60): the clock movers run on.\n- `onStep(f: () => void, o: { first?: boolean } = {}): () => void`: Run `f` after every fixed step, before bound meshes (`bind`) read their bodies. Listeners run in the order they were added (instanced bodies keep their last two poses, a ragdoll holds its join\n- `addMover(body: KinematicBody, options: MoverOptions): Mover`: Drive a kinematic body (`RigidBodyDesc.kinematicPositionBased()`) along a path, spinning or swinging, as a pure function of its own clock (physics/movers.ts), which starts at 0 now: the same howe\n- `conveyor(collider: RAPIER.Collider, velocity: readonly [number, number, number] | null): void`: Make a collider a conveyor belt moving at `velocity` (m/s, world axes): dynamic bodies touching it are dragged along, the character standing on it is carried.\n- `beltVelocity(handle: number): readonly [number, number, number] | null`: A conveyor's velocity, by collider handle (null: not a belt).\n- `explode(at: readonly [number, number, number] | Vector3, o: ExplosionOptions = {}): number`: Push every dynamic body near `at` away from it (physics/forces.ts). Returns how many.\n- `bind(body: RAPIER.RigidBody, object: Object3D): void`: Make `object` follow `body` (interpolated).\n- `unbind(object: Object3D): void`\n- `addStaticBox(o: BoxOptions): RAPIER.Collider`\n- `addStaticCylinder(position: [number, number, number], halfHeight: number, radius: number): RAPIER.Collider`\n- `addDynamicBox(o: BoxOptions): RAPIER.RigidBody`\n- `tag(collider: RAPIER.Collider, ...tags: string[]): RAPIER.Collider`: Tag a collider with gameplay semantics the character controller understands: 'climbable' (ladders/vines), 'pushable', 'grabbable', 'slippery', 'noLedge', 'character', 'noCamera' (camera ra\n- `hasTag(collider: RAPIER.Collider | null | undefined, tag: string): boolean`\n- `raycast(from: Vector3, dir: Vector3, maxDistance: number, ignoreTags: readonly string[] = NO_TAGS): number | null`: Distance along `dir` (unit) from `from` to the first collider not carrying any of `ignoreTags`.\n- `castRay(from: Vector3, dir: Vector3, maxDistance: number, ignoreTags: readonly string[] = NO_TAGS, exclude?: RAPIER.RigidBody): { distance: number; collider: RAPIER.Collider; normal: Vector3; point: Vector3 } | null`: Ray cast returning distance, hit collid\n- `castUp(x: number, y: number, z: number, maxDistance: number, out: { y: number; nx: number; ny: number; nz: number; id: number }, ignoreTags: readonly string[] = NO_TAGS, exclude?: RAPIER.RigidBody): boolean`: Straight up from (x, y, z), at most `maxDistance\n- `castDown(x: number, y: number, z: number, maxDistance: number, out: { y: number; nx: number; ny: number; nz: number; id: number }, ignoreTags: readonly string[] = NO_TAGS, exclude?: RAPIER.RigidBody): boolean`: Straight down from (x, y, z), at most `maxDist\n- `groundBelow(origin: Vector3, maxDistance = 20, exclude?: RAPIER.RigidBody): { y: number; distance: number } | null`: Distance straight down from `origin` to the first collider (excluding `exclude`).\n- `trigger(shape: TriggerShape, at: readonly [number, number, number] | Vector3, options: TriggerOptions = {}): Trigger`: A trigger volume with enter/exit callbacks (pickups, checkpoints, kill zones, doors). Checked after every fixed step against dynamic and k\n- `updateTriggers(): void`: Run every trigger's overlap query now (Physics.update does this after each step).\n- `isAlive(target: { isValid(): boolean }): boolean`: Whether `target` (a body, collider or joint) still exists in the current world: false once removed, and for anything from a level before (its world is gone; `isValid()` would throw).\n- `remove(target: RAPIER.RigidBody | RAPIER.Collider): void`: Remove a rigid body (with its colliders and any bound Object3D binding) or a single collider. Removing a collider whose fixed body has no other colliders removes that body too (what `addStaticBox` &\n- `clear(): void`: Empty the world: every body, collider, joint, character and vehicle controller, trigger, tag, binding, mover, field and belt goes; gravity and the solver's iterations go back to their defaults, the step accumulator and the step count reset. \n- `fingerprint(): string`: A hash of the physics state: every body (position, rotation, velocities, asleep, enabled) and collider (pose, friction, restitution, sensor, enabled), exact, plus the step count and the time not yet stepped. Two runs that should be t\n- `counts(): { bodies: number; colliders: number; joints: number; tags: number; bindings: number; triggers: number; controllers: number; vehicles: number; movers: number; fields: number; belts: number; }`: Sizes of everything Physics tracks (leak checks, debug\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n\n### interface RagdollOptions\n\n- `density?: number`: World density of the parts (the world's mass units per m³). Default 3.\n- `damping?: number`: Linear and angular damping (air drag, joint friction). Defaults 0.1 and 1.5.\n- `angularDamping?: number`\n- `friction?: number`: Friction of the parts on the ground. Default 0.5.\n\n\n### interface DecalOptions\n\n- `size?: number`: Width of the mark (m). Default 0.5.\n- `rotation?: number`: Turn about the normal (radians). Default random.\n- `color?: number`: Colour (hex). Default dark.\n- `life?: number`: Seconds before it starts to fade (0: forever). Default 10.\n\n\n### interface PlayerSettings\n\nThe player's settings: the standard picture and engine options every game gets, as plain data\n(sound is the AudioManager's, which keeps its own volumes). A field left out is the game's own\nchoice; a field set is the player's and wins over it. `engine.settings` holds them, applies\nthem, saves them per game and shows them in the settings panel (the ⚙ button).\n\n- `look?: string`: A LOOK_PRESETS name. Left out: the look the game gives each level.\n- `pixelArt?: boolean`: Pixel art (the pixel pass), or false for smooth 3D (render mode `raw`).\n- `pixelSize?: 'fine' | 'chunky'`: The art resolution: `fine` (the game's, 480×270 by default) or `chunky` (two thirds of it: bigger pixels).\n- `quality?: QualityOption`: Shadow and light quality: a level, or `auto` (the device's).\n- `fps?: number`: Frame cap: 60, 30, or 0 for the display's own rate.\n- `debugInfo?: boolean`: The debug panel: frame rate, camera, GPU errors and the game's status.\n\n\n### interface Spatial\n\n- `gain: number`: 0..1 volume.\n- `pan: number`: -1 (left) .. 1 (right).\n- `distance: number`\n\n\n### interface SpatialOptions\n\n- `ref?: number`: Within this distance (m) the sound is at full volume (default 1).\n- `max?: number`: Silent from this distance on (default 30); it fades out over the last fifth.\n- `rolloff?: number`: How fast it falls off past `ref` (default 1: inverse distance, the way sound really does).\n\n\n### interface Listener\n\n- `position: V3Like`\n- `right: V3Like`: The listener's right, in world space (unit): the camera's right for a third-person game.\n\n\n### class ScreenFx\n\n- `cover(kind: TransitionKind = 'fade', o: TransitionOptions = {}): Promise<boolean>`: Cover the picture (progress → 1). Resolves when it stops: `true` when it is fully covered, `false` when another transition (or `set`, `clear`) took over first.\n- `reveal(kind?: TransitionKind, o: TransitionOptions = {}): Promise<boolean>`: Uncover it (progress → 0) with `kind` (default: the one that covered it). Resolves like `cover`.\n- `transition(kind: TransitionKind, between: () => unknown, o: TransitionOptions & { revealCenter?: TransitionOptions['center'] } = {}): Promise<boolean>`: Cover, run `between` (load a level, teleport), then reveal, also when `between` throws (the error is pas\n- `set(kind: TransitionKind | null, progress: number): void`: Jump straight to a progress (0 clear, 1 covered), no animation.\n- `flash(color: ScreenColor = 'white', o: FlashOptions = {}): void`: A full-screen flash that fades out.\n- `shockwave(at: Vector3 | readonly [number, number], o: ShockwaveOptions = {}): void`: A ring that pushes the picture outwards from `at` (oldest ring is replaced when 4 run).\n- `clear(): void`: Stop everything (a clear picture).\n- `state(): ScreenFxState`\n- `update(dt: number, camera: Camera | null): void`: Engine, every rendered frame (real seconds; `camera` projects world centres).\n- `sampleNode(tex: any, scale: any): any`: Sample an art-resolution picture for the device pass, pushed by the shockwaves and blocked up by a mosaic transition, with the rings' bright edge. `tex` is the art target (a texture node); `scale` is device pixels per\n- `colorNode(color: any, scale: any): any`: The transition and the flash over a finished colour (device pass).\n\n\n### beltMaterial()\n\n```ts\nfunction beltMaterial(base: number, stripe: number, o: { length: number; speed: number; pitch?: number; along?: 'u' | 'v' }): BeltMaterial\n```\n\n\n### hudSprite()\n\n```ts\nfunction hudSprite(idOrDef: string | TextureDef, o: TextureOptions & { frame?: number } = {}): { rows: string[]; colors: Record<string, PaletteColor | number> }\n```\n\nOne frame as `hud.sprite` rows and colours: a character per slot (a, b, c, … in palette order),\n'.' for transparent.\n\n  const s = hudSprite('gem-icon'); hud.sprite(8, 8, s.rows, s.colors, { scale: 2 });\n\n\n### buildModel()\n\n```ts\nfunction buildModel(idOrDef: string | ModelDef, opts: ModelOptions = {}): ModelBuild\n```\n\n\n### interface ModelBuild\n\n- `readonly id: string`\n- `readonly object: Group`: Named after the model; pivots are named Groups inside it.\n- `readonly bounds: Bounds`\n- `readonly anchors: Readonly<Record<string, { readonly at: Vec3; readonly rot: Vec3 }>>`\n- `readonly colliders: readonly ColliderData[]`\n- `readonly light: ModelLightRequest | null`\n- `readonly report: ModelReport`\n\n\n### addModelColliders()\n\n```ts\nfunction addModelColliders(physics: Physics, build: Pick<ModelBuild, 'colliders'>, at: Vec3 = [0, 0, 0], yaw = 0): RAPIER.Collider[]\n```\n\nStatic Rapier colliders for a placed model (its `colliders` data), at `at` turned `yaw`\nradians about Y: a box, an upright cylinder or a convex hull, with `addStaticBox`'s friction.\n\n\n### mergeStaticMeshes()\n\n```ts\nfunction mergeStaticMeshes(sources: readonly Object3D[], options: MergeOptions = {}): Mesh[]\n```\n\nMerge static meshes into one mesh per (material, shadow flags): N blocks with M\nmaterials become ≤ M draw calls instead of N × groups (a BoxGeometry with 6 material\ngroups is 6 draws, plus 6 more in the shadow pass).\n\nWorld transforms are baked into the vertices, multi-material geometry is split by its\ngroups, and `position` + `normal` are kept, plus `uv` under a material with a `map` and\n`color` under one with `vertexColors` (what toon materials read). The\nsources are left untouched (don't add them to the scene). Physics is separate: keep\none collider per block. Merged meshes are culled as a whole, so merge things that are\non screen together (a level, a room), and keep anything that moves…\n\n\n### interface MergeOptions\n\n- `castShadow?: boolean`: Override castShadow on every merged mesh (default: keep each source mesh's flag).\n- `receiveShadow?: boolean`: Override receiveShadow on every merged mesh (default: keep each source mesh's flag).\n\n\n### class Rng\n\nSeeded randomness. Everything random in a game comes from an `Rng`, so the same seed always\ngives the same result (docs/DOCTRINE.md, principle 1). Each level gets one, `ctx.random`,\nseeded from the engine's seed and the game's name; fork it by purpose so streams stay\nindependent of how many numbers each one drew:\n\n  const level = ctx.random.fork(`level:${n}`);\n  const room = level.fork(`room:${i}`);   // independent of how many numbers `level` drew\n\nNever use Math.random in game or engine code (the lint refuses it).\n\n- `new Rng(seed: number | string)`\n- `get state: number`: The generator's whole state: save it, and set it back to draw the same numbers again.\n- `next(): number`: Uniform in [0, 1). mulberry32.\n- `fork(purpose: string | number): Rng`: A child generator for one purpose; does not advance this one.\n- `range(min: number, max: number): number`: Float in [min, max).\n- `int(min: number, max: number): number`: Integer in [min, max] (inclusive).\n- `chance(p: number): boolean`\n- `pick(items: readonly T[]): T`\n- `weighted(items: readonly T[], weight: (item: T) => number): T`: Pick by weight; entries with weight <= 0 never come up.\n- `shuffle(items: T[]): T[]`\n- `gaussian(mean = 0, sd = 1): number`: Normal distribution (Box–Muller).\n\n\n### class Hud\n\nPixel HUD: crisp text and icons drawn in art pixels on top of the game, never through\nthe post filters. It is a 2D canvas at the internal resolution (480×270 / 320×180),\nlaid over the game canvas with the same integer scale and letterbox offset\n(`framing.ts`), so one HUD pixel is exactly one art pixel at every resolution.\n\nRetained: what you add stays on screen until `clear()`. Redraw everything each frame\n(clear + add) or only when something changes; the canvas repaints only when the content,\nresolution or framing changed. Available as `ctx.hud`.\n\n  ctx.hud.clear();\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, `COINS ${n}/12`, { color: 'sand' });\n  ctx.hud.text(4, 4, 'PAUSED', { anchor: 'center', scale: 2 });\n\n- `new Hud(container: HTMLElement | null)`\n- `canvas: HTMLCanvasElement | null`: The overlay canvas (created on the first draw; null when nothing was ever drawn).\n- `visible: boolean`\n- `get width: number`: HUD width/height in art pixels (the internal resolution).\n- `get height: number`\n- `text(x: number, y: number, text: string, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: Text in the 5×7 bitmap font (uppercase; digits and common punctuation).\n- `rect(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, color: HudColor, anchor: HudAnchor = 'top-left'): void`: A filled rectangle (panels, bars).\n- `sprite(x: number, y: number, rows: readonly string[], colors: Record<string, HudColor>, options: HudOptions = {}): void`: A tiny pixel-art icon as data: one string per row, one character per pixel, mapped through `colors` ('.' or ' ' = transparent).\n- `clear(): void`: Remove everything.\n- `measure(text: string, scale = 1): { width: number; height: number }`: Size of `text` in art pixels at `scale`.\n- `sync(resolution: Resolution, framing: Framing): void`: Engine: follow the renderer's resolution and framing, and repaint if needed.\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n\n### hudPlace()\n\n```ts\nfunction hudPlace(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, anchor: HudAnchor, size: Resolution): [number, number]\n```\n\nTop-left corner, in whole art pixels, of a w×h element placed at offset (x, y) from\n`anchor` on a screen of `size` art pixels. Pure (unit-tested).\n\n{\"fps\":30,\"root\":\"Pelvis\",\"joints\":[\"Pelvis\",\"Torso\",\"Head\",\"ArmR\",\"ForearmR\",\"HandR\",\"ArmL\",\"ForearmL\",\"HandL\",\"LegR\",\"ShinR\",\"FootR\",\"LegL\",\"ShinL\",\"FootL\"],\"mirror\":{\"ArmR\":\"ArmL\",\"ArmL\":\"ArmR\",\"ForearmR\":\"ForearmL\",\"ForearmL\":\"ForearmR\",\"HandR\":\"HandL\",\"HandL\":\"HandR\",\"LegR\":\"LegL\",\"LegL\":\"LegR\",\"ShinR\":\"ShinL\",\"ShinL\":\"ShinR\",\"FootR\":\"FootL\",\"FootL\":\"FootR\"},\"soles\":[\"ShoeR\",\"ShoeL\"],\"trace\":[\"GloveR\",\"GloveL\",\"ShoeR\",\"ShoeL\",\"Head\"],\"limits\":{\"ShinR\":{\"x\":[-3,165]},\"ShinL\":{\"x\":[-3,165]},\"ForearmR\":{\"x\":[-160,5]},\"ForearmL\":{\"x\":[-160,5]},\"Head\":{\"x\":[-60,70],\"y\":[-95,95],\"z\":[-45,45]},\"FootR\":{\"x\":[-80,80]},\"FootL\":{\"x\":[-80,80]},\"HandR\":{\"x\":[-90,70]},\"HandL\":{\"x\":[-90,70]},\"Torso\":{\"x\":[-50,90],\"y\":[-70,70],\"z\":[-45,45]}},\"legs\":{\"R\":{\"upper\":\"LegR\",\"lower\":\"ShinR\",\"foot\":\"FootR\",\"hip\":[-0.14,0,0]},\"L\":{\"upper\":\"LegL\",\"lower\":\"ShinL\",\"foot\":\"FootL\",\"hip\":[0.14,0,0]},\"rootHeight\":0.62,\"upper\":0.3,\"lower\":0.22,\"ankle\":0.1,\"heel\":0.11,\"ball\":0.21,\"top\":0.02},\"spine\":{\"torso\":\"Torso\",\"head\":\"Head\",\"cap\":\"Cap\"}}\nIdle:60L IdleLook:102L Teeter:30L Tiptoe:18L Walk:12L Run:12L Skid:18 SkidTurn:12 StepUp:8 StepDown:8 Crouch:40L CrouchWalk:12L CrouchSlide:20L ProneDown:16 Prone:60L Crawl:36L GetUpFront:21 Sit:60L SitDown:16 StandUp:16 LieDown:30 LieIdle:60L Sleep:90L GetUp:24 Jump:20 JumpUp:20 DoubleJump:22 TripleJump:30 Backflip:30 SideFlip:26 LongJump:36 WallKick:20 WallSlide:20L Fall:16L Dive:12 BellySlide:20L GroundPoundSpin:9 GroundPound:10 GroundPoundLand:15 Land:10 HardLand:30 Slide:20L Hang:40L ShimmyRight:20L ShimmyLeft:20L PullUp:27 ClimbIdle:40L Climb:24L Push:30L PushIdle:40L Grab:40L Pull:30L Punch:10 Punch2:10 Kick:14 SweepKick:18 JumpKick:14 Wave:44 Victory:48 Hurt:20 Slash1:12 Slash2:12 Slash3:18 Slam:24 LeapSlam:28 Spin:12L Cast:16 CastBig:22 CastWeapon:16 CastBigWeapon:22 BowDraw:18 BowRelease:12 Roll:14 Charge:14 Shout:20 HitReact:10 Death:36 Triumph:40\n{\"name\":\"Kick\",\"fast\":true,\"frames\":14,\"grounded\":true,\"keys\":[[0,{\"Pelvis\":{\"r\":[0,0,0],\"p\":[0,-0.07,0],\"s\":1},\"Torso\":[8,0,0],\"Head\":[-6,0,0],\"ArmR\":[-40,0,-16],\"ForearmR\":[-115,0,0],\"HandR\":[-10,0,0],\"ArmL\":[-48,0,16],\"ForearmL\":[-120,0,0],\"HandL\":[-10,0,0],\"LegR\":{\"r\":[-7.388,0,0],\"p\":[0,0,0],\"s\":[1,1,1]},\"ShinR\":{\"r\":[53.509,0,0],\"p\":[0,0,0],\"s\":[1,1,1]},\"FootR\":{\"r\":[-46.121,0,0],\"p\":[0,0,0],\"s\":[1,1,1]},\"LegL\":{\"r\":[-38.441,0,0],\"p\":[0,0,0],\"s\":[1,1,1]},\"ShinL\":{\"r\":[50.647,0,0],\"p\":[0,0,0],\"s\":[1,1,1]},\"FootL\":{\"r\":[-12.206,0,0],\"p\":[0,0,0],\"s\":[1,1,1]}},null],[4,{\"Pelvis\":{\"r\":[0,0,0],\"p\":[0,-0.07,0],\"s\":1},\"Torso\":[-6,0,0],\"Head\":[-6,0,0],\"ArmR\":[-30,0,-50],\"ForearmR\":[-60,0,0],\"HandR\":[0,0,0],\"ArmL\":[-60,0,40],\"ForearmL\":[-60,0,0],\"HandL\":[0,0,0],\"LegR\":[-85,0,-5],\"ShinR\":[110,0,0],\"FootR\":[20,0,0],\"LegL\":{\"r\":[-38.441,0,0],\"p\":[0,0,0],\"s\":[1,1,1]},\"ShinL\":{\"r\":[50.647,0,0],\"p\n[{\"bone\":\"Pelvis\",\"from\":[-0.12,-0.04,0],\"to\":[0.12,-0.04,0],\"radius\":0.13},{\"bone\":\"Torso\",\"parent\":\"Pelvis\",\"from\":[0,0.16,0],\"to\":[0,0.42,0],\"radius\":0.2,\"cone\":35},{\"bone\":\"Head\",\"parent\":\"Torso\",\"from\":[0,0.2,0],\"to\":[0,0.34,0],\"radius\":0.22,\"cone\":40,\"density\":0.7},{\"bone\":\"ArmR\",\"parent\":\"Torso\",\"to\":[0,-0.25,0],\"radius\":0.07,\"cone\":100},{\"bone\":\"ForearmR\",\"parent\":\"ArmR\",\"to\":[0,-0.26,0],\"radius\":0.07,\"hinge\":[-150,0]},{\"bone\":\"ArmL\",\"parent\":\"Torso\",\"to\":[0,-0.25,0],\"radius\":0.07,\"cone\"\n","numLines":498,"startLine":1,"totalLines":498}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011mXo4tzbfqk8hDnXc4zg78","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
