{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkmKAF16Mx5kTnyFiPp5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012dvuQAihLwoJuSFreruuU8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'P'\np='src/screens/pause.js';s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"ui.dim(); ui.center(36, 'PAUSED', { scale: 2, color: 'sand' }); ui.center(58, A.objective, { color: 'mist' });\",\"ui.dim(); ui.rect(0, 26, ui.W, ui.H - 62, 'ink'); ui.center(36, 'PAUSED', { scale: 2, color: 'sand' }); ui.center(58, A.objective, { color: 'mist' });\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/game/hud.js';s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"if (A.needClick && !A.attract) ui.center(H / 2 + 24, 'CLICK TO AIM', { color: 'sand' });\",\"if (A.needClick && !A.attract && A.app.dtShown !== false) ui.center(H - 60, 'CLICK TO AIM', { color: 'sand' });\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='tests/browser/browser.py';s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"def page(b, url=html, init=None, **kw):\"\"\",\"\"\"TAP = '''(() => { const orig = AudioNode.prototype.connect; AudioNode.prototype.connect = function (d, ...r) { if (d instanceof AudioDestinationNode) { const c = d.context; if (!c.__an) { c.__an = c.createAnalyser(); c.__an.fftSize = 2048; orig.call(c.__an, d); window.__ctx = c; } orig.call(this, c.__an); return d; } return orig.call(this, d, ...r); }; window.__peak = () => { const a = window.__ctx?.__an; if (!a) return -1; const b = new Float32Array(a.fftSize); a.getFloatTimeDomainData(b); let m = 0; for (const v of b) m = Math.max(m, Math.abs(v)); return m; }; })()'''\ndef page(b, url=html, init=None, **kw):\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"        pg, ctx = page(b); wait_title(pg); pg.wait_for_timeout(800)\n        ok(not pg.errs, 'boots with no console errors'\"\"\",\"\"\"        pg, ctx = page(b, init=TAP); wait_title(pg); pg.wait_for_timeout(800)\n        ok(not pg.errs, 'boots with no console errors'\"\"\")\na=s.index(\"        pg.keyboard.press('ArrowDown'); pg.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        lvl = \"); b=s.index(\"        st = pg.evaluate('''()=>{const a=window.__APP__;a.settings.music=0.5\")\ns=s[:a]+\"\"\"        pg.keyboard.press('ArrowDown'); pg.evaluate('window.__APP__.mix.play(\"title\",0.1); window.__e.audio.playMusic(null); window.__APP__.mix.current=null; window.__APP__.mix.play(\"title\",0.1)'); peak = 0\n        for _ in range(40):\n            pg.wait_for_timeout(150); peak = max(peak, pg.evaluate('window.__peak()'))\n        ok(peak > 0.002, 'music is audible at 10 percent on the bus', peak); ok(peak < 0.5, 'and not loud', peak)\n\"\"\"+s[b:]\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"ok(abs(st-0.5)<0.01, 'music setting applies', st)\"\"\",\"\"\"ok(abs(st-0.5)<0.01, 'music setting applies', st); r = pg.evaluate('''(async()=>{const a=window.__APP__;Object.assign(a.settings,{music:0.1});a.applySettings();return window.__e.audio.volume.music})()'''); ok(abs(r-0.1)<0.01, 'reset returns to 10 percent', r)\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nP\ncat > index.html <<'E'\n<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>dev page</title></head><body><div id=\"app\"></div><script type=\"module\" src=\"./src/main.js\"></script></body></html>\nE\ncat > docs/CONTENT.md <<'E'\n# Adding content without touching systems\n\nAn area is a data module. Everything below lives in `src/data/`.\n\n## An area\nAdd painter commands to `levels/maps.js`: `map name W H fill`, then `R x0 y0 x1 y1 c`, `B x0 y0 x1 y1 wall floor`, `P x y c`. One set of rows gives geometry, colliders, nav and the Map tab. Characters and markers are the plan's table: `#` stone, `T` timber, `~` deep water, `H` low cover, `D` door, `W` window, `G` gate, `S` shutter, `B` crate, `c` belt, `%` shallows; `a` start, `1-5` spawn doors, `m` Mr. Fathom, `t` telegraph, `y` Tannoy, `$` chest.\n\nThen add an entry to `levels/areas.js`:\n```js\nmyarea: { map: 'myarea', title: 'THE PLACE', mood: 'rain', music: 'explore', chapter: 3, first: 'main',\n  treasure: ['pearl'], barrels: [[4, 5]], groundItems: [['samphire', 6, 7, 1]], notes: [{ id: 'hymn', col: 2, row: 3 }],\n  decor: [['crate', 3, 4]], props: [['barrel', 5, 5]], lamps: [['lamp-post', 8, 8]], hideSpots: [[9, 9, 'barrel']],\n  dress: { wall: ['barrel'], open: ['puddle'] }, backdrops: [['backdrop-cliff', 40, -3, 0]],\n  stages: { main: [ /* steps */ ], next: [ /* steps */ ] } }\n```\nAdd it to `TELEPORTS` for dev mode and to `CHAPTER_OF`. Bot goals for the whole-game test go in `BOT_GOALS` in `game/bot.js`.\n\n## Steps (the beat language: `game/director.js`)\n`{ wait: 2 }` · `{ until: (a) => cond }` · `{ zone: [col0, row0, col1, row1] }` · `{ run: (a) => {} }` · `{ scene: 'name', shots: [...], duration }` a cutscene with the lines of `SCENES.name` · `{ lines: 'name' }` radio subtitles · `{ say: ['MAX', 'Noted.'] }` · `{ objective: 'TEXT' }` · `{ hint: 'aim' }` · `{ radio: 'tide' }` · `{ music: 'siege' }` (`null` is silence) · `{ flag: 'x' }` · `{ spawn: [['gaffer', col, row, opts]] }` · `{ wave: { groups: [['gaffer', 10]], doors: '123', every: 2, maxActive: 8 } }` then `{ waitWave: true }` · `{ openGate: 'G' }` · `{ checkpoint: true }` · `{ stage: 'next' }`.\n\nA stage is a stretch of story. Entering one saves a checkpoint, and reloading restarts that stage: restore anything it needs in its first step.\n\n## An enemy\nAdd to `enemies.js`: hp, speed, dmg, windup, reach, gait, model, and flags (`grab`, `throws`, `shield`, `armoured`, `heavy`, `crawler`, `saw`, `targetDame`). Add a puppet with `puppet(id, about, palette, extras)` in `models/humans.js`. Add it to `SPAWNABLE` for dev mode. New behaviour: an `s_STATE(dt)` method on the Enemy (or on one instance).\n\n## A weapon\nAdd to `weapons.js` and `WEAPON_ORDER`, an item in `items.js`, a model in `models/weapons.js` with its barrel along +Z (map it in `MODEL_OF`, `player.js`), and a shop entry in `shop.js`. `pellets`, `cone`, `falloff`, `pierce`, `pin`, `scope`, `popChance` are data.\n\n## An item\nAdd to `items.js` (`kind`: herb, ammo, grenade, treasure, key; `w`, `h`, `price`, `about`) and an icon in `models/icons.js`, sized 14 art pixels a cell. Recipes are `combineRecipes`.\n\n## A line\nAll writing is `dialogue.js`. HUD font only: uppercase letters, digits, common punctuation. `tests/node/units.mjs` scans every string. Add a speaker's colour to `COLORS` and a voice recipe in `audio/voice.js`.\n\n## A song or a sound\nSong data in `audio/songs.js` (validated by `parseSong`), sound data in `audio/sfx.js` (rendered and checked for silence and clipping).\n\n## Balance\n`tuning.js` is what the dev sliders change. Weapons, enemies and prices are data. Run `node tests/node/playthrough.mjs --v` for the balance report.\nE\nnode tools/build.mjs | tail -1; timeout 120 python3 tests/browser/browser.py boot 2>&1 | grep -v \"^  \\|^    \\|Traceback\\|\\^\" | tail -4 | cut -c1-300; timeout 170 node check.mjs --keys KeyW*60,KeyD*40 2>&1 | tail -6 | cut -c1-220","description":"Polish pause, audio bus test, content docs, kit check on dev page","timeout":320000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2953,"cache_read_input_tokens":728096,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2953},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76d12802-c986-437e-adae-1ae347966275","uuid":"4484ac55-87c3-4aad-873b-7b0b941d3b45","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:57:08.999Z","request_id":"req_011CgkmK9rgr5kkmSewzPcrA","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012dvuQAihLwoJuSFreruuU8":{"command":"python3 - <<'P'\np='src/screens/pause.js';s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"ui.dim(); ui.center(36, 'PAUSED', { scale: 2, color: 'sand' }); ui.center(58, A.objective, { color: 'mist' });\",\"ui.dim(); ui.rect(0, 26, ui.W, ui.H - 62, 'ink'); ui.center(36, 'PAUSED', { scale: 2, color: 'sand' }); ui.center(58, A.objective, { color: 'mist' });\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/game/hud.js';s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"if (A.needClick && !A.attract) ui.center(H / 2 + 24, 'CLICK TO AIM', { color: 'sand' });\",\"if (A.needClick && !A.attract && A.app.dtShown !== false) ui.center(H - 60, 'CLICK TO AIM', { color: 'sand' });\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='tests/browser/browser.py';s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"def page(b, url=html, init=None, **kw):\"\"\",\"\"\"TAP = '''(() => { const orig = AudioNode.prototype.connect; AudioNode.prototype.connect = function (d, ...r) { if (d instanceof AudioDestinationNode) { const c = d.context; if (!c.__an) { c.__an = c.createAnalyser(); c.__an.fftSize = 2048; orig.call(c.__an, d); window.__ctx = c; } orig.call(this, c.__an); return d; } return orig.call(this, d, ...r); }; window.__peak = () => { const a = window.__ctx?.__an; if (!a) return -1; const b = new Float32Array(a.fftSize); a.getFloatTimeDomainData(b); let m = 0; for (const v of b) m = Math.max(m, Math.abs(v)); return m; }; })()'''\ndef page(b, url=html, init=None, **kw):\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"        pg, ctx = page(b); wait_title(pg); pg.wait_for_timeout(800)\n        ok(not pg.errs, 'boots with no console errors'\"\"\",\"\"\"        pg, ctx = page(b, init=TAP); wait_title(pg); pg.wait_for_timeout(800)\n        ok(not pg.errs, 'boots with no console errors'\"\"\")\na=s.index(\"        pg.keyboard.press('ArrowDown'); pg.wait_for_timeout(300)\\n        lvl = \"); b=s.index(\"        st = pg.evaluate('''()=>{const a=window.__APP__;a.settings.music=0.5\")\ns=s[:a]+\"\"\"        pg.keyboard.press('ArrowDown'); pg.evaluate('window.__APP__.mix.play(\"title\",0.1); window.__e.audio.playMusic(null); window.__APP__.mix.current=null; window.__APP__.mix.play(\"title\",0.1)'); peak = 0\n        for _ in range(40):\n            pg.wait_for_timeout(150); peak = max(peak, pg.evaluate('window.__peak()'))\n        ok(peak > 0.002, 'music is audible at 10 percent on the bus', peak); ok(peak < 0.5, 'and not loud', peak)\n\"\"\"+s[b:]\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"ok(abs(st-0.5)<0.01, 'music setting applies', st)\"\"\",\"\"\"ok(abs(st-0.5)<0.01, 'music setting applies', st); r = pg.evaluate('''(async()=>{const a=window.__APP__;Object.assign(a.settings,{music:0.1});a.applySettings();return window.__e.audio.volume.music})()'''); ok(abs(r-0.1)<0.01, 'reset returns to 10 percent', r)\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nP\ncat > index.html <<'E'\n<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><title>dev page</title></head><body><div id=\"app\"></div><script type=\"module\" src=\"./src/main.js\"></script></body></html>\nE\ncat > docs/CONTENT.md <<'E'\n# Adding content without touching systems\n\nAn area is a data module. Everything below lives in `src/data/`.\n\n## An area\nAdd painter commands to `levels/maps.js`: `map name W H fill`, then `R x0 y0 x1 y1 c`, `B x0 y0 x1 y1 wall floor`, `P x y c`. One set of rows gives geometry, colliders, nav and the Map tab. Characters and markers are the plan's table: `#` stone, `T` timber, `~` deep water, `H` low cover, `D` door, `W` window, `G` gate, `S` shutter, `B` crate, `c` belt, `%` shallows; `a` start, `1-5` spawn doors, `m` Mr. Fathom, `t` telegraph, `y` Tannoy, `$` chest.\n\nThen add an entry to `levels/areas.js`:\n```js\nmyarea: { map: 'myarea', title: 'THE PLACE', mood: 'rain', music: 'explore', chapter: 3, first: 'main',\n  treasure: ['pearl'], barrels: [[4, 5]], groundItems: [['samphire', 6, 7, 1]], notes: [{ id: 'hymn', col: 2, row: 3 }],\n  decor: [['crate', 3, 4]], props: [['barrel', 5, 5]], lamps: [['lamp-post', 8, 8]], hideSpots: [[9, 9, 'barrel']],\n  dress: { wall: ['barrel'], open: ['puddle'] }, backdrops: [['backdrop-cliff', 40, -3, 0]],\n  stages: { main: [ /* steps */ ], next: [ /* steps */ ] } }\n```\nAdd it to `TELEPORTS` for dev mode and to `CHAPTER_OF`. Bot goals for the whole-game test go in `BOT_GOALS` in `game/bot.js`.\n\n## Steps (the beat language: `game/director.js`)\n`{ wait: 2 }` · `{ until: (a) => cond }` · `{ zone: [col0, row0, col1, row1] }` · `{ run: (a) => {} }` · `{ scene: 'name', shots: [...], duration }` a cutscene with the lines of `SCENES.name` · `{ lines: 'name' }` radio subtitles · `{ say: ['MAX', 'Noted.'] }` · `{ objective: 'TEXT' }` · `{ hint: 'aim' }` · `{ radio: 'tide' }` · `{ music: 'siege' }` (`null` is silence) · `{ flag: 'x' }` · `{ spawn: [['gaffer', col, row, opts]] }` · `{ wave: { groups: [['gaffer', 10]], doors: '123', every: 2, maxActive: 8 } }` then `{ waitWave: true }` · `{ openGate: 'G' }` · `{ checkpoint: true }` · `{ stage: 'next' }`.\n\nA stage is a stretch of story. Entering one saves a checkpoint, and reloading restarts that stage: restore anything it needs in its first step.\n\n## An enemy\nAdd to `enemies.js`: hp, speed, dmg, windup, reach, gait, model, and flags (`grab`, `throws`, `shield`, `armoured`, `heavy`, `crawler`, `saw`, `targetDame`). Add a puppet with `puppet(id, about, palette, extras)` in `models/humans.js`. Add it to `SPAWNABLE` for dev mode. New behaviour: an `s_STATE(dt)` method on the Enemy (or on one instance).\n\n## A weapon\nAdd to `weapons.js` and `WEAPON_ORDER`, an item in `items.js`, a model in `models/weapons.js` with its barrel along +Z (map it in `MODEL_OF`, `player.js`), and a shop entry in `shop.js`. `pellets`, `cone`, `falloff`, `pierce`, `pin`, `scope`, `popChance` are data.\n\n## An item\nAdd to `items.js` (`kind`: herb, ammo, grenade, treasure, key; `w`, `h`, `price`, `about`) and an icon in `models/icons.js`, sized 14 art pixels a cell. Recipes are `combineRecipes`.\n\n## A line\nAll writing is `dialogue.js`. HUD font only: uppercase letters, digits, common punctuation. `tests/node/units.mjs` scans every string. Add a speaker's colour to `COLORS` and a voice recipe in `audio/voice.js`.\n\n## A song or a sound\nSong data in `audio/songs.js` (validated by `parseSong`), sound data in `audio/sfx.js` (rendered and checked for silence and clipping).\n\n## Balance\n`tuning.js` is what the dev sliders change. Weapons, enemies and prices are data. Run `node tests/node/playthrough.mjs --v` for the balance report.\nE\nnode tools/build.mjs | tail -1; timeout 120 python3 tests/browser/browser.py boot 2>&1 | grep -v \"^  \\|^    \\|Traceback\\|\\^\" | tail -4 | cut -c1-300; timeout 170 node check.mjs --keys KeyW*60,KeyD*40 2>&1 | tail -6 | cut -c1-220","description":"Polish pause, audio bus test, content docs, kit check on dev page","timeout":320000}}}
