{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkmXoTTjWtaqMXBq7yDw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XkEmEnyjCVYboWjvsS5LC5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'P'\np='src/game/launch.js';s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"P.noMove = true; this.run.health =\",\"P.noMove = true; this.infiniteAmmo = true; this.run.health =\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/data/about.js';s=open(p).read()\nimport re\na=s.index(\"export const TESTING_FEEDBACK\"); b=s.index(\"export const CREDITS\")\nnew = r\"\"\"export const TESTING_FEEDBACK = [\n  ['How many issues did testing catch?', 'About 35 real issues: roughly 20 from the whole-game bot playthrough, 3 from the node suites, 12 from browser and harness runs. Many more were bugs in the bot or the tests themselves, which I do not count.'],\n  ['How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?', 'About 12. Reloading a checkpoint lost the nested story script and left the game stuck. Set pieces changed shared level data, which broke every retry. A checkpoint taken mid-vault put you inside a wall. Gate opening crashed. The road had no door action, so no way forward. The final boss valves could not be hit. Launch mines sat under the ground collider. Opening the Case with Triangle dropped your gun. Esc and I opened a menu and shut it in the same frame. Menu taps were lost at low frame rates. Hub traffic starved when rendering was slow.'],\n  ['What was the most helpful test you ran?', 'The scripted whole-game playthrough in Node. It runs about 60 times faster than real time, so one run of the entire game took under a minute and it found most of the game-breaking bugs.'],\n  ['What was the least helpful test you ran?', 'The per-sound render checks and the model checks. They all stayed green after the first fix. They guard against typos, but they never found a gameplay problem.'],\n];\nexport const ENGINE_FEEDBACK = [\n  ['What did you like most about the engine?', 'Engine.headless. The same game code runs in Node with no GPU, deterministic and very fast, so a bot can play the whole game. A close second is writing models, textures and clips as plain data.'],\n  ['Did you get stuck or guess wrong?', 'A few times. One model id clashed with the library (armchair) and the catalog threw. shelf is not an id, it is bookshelf. TEXTURE_LIBRARY.get throws rather than returning null. Pad presses are dropped at time scale 0, so I had to read pads myself in menus. A full-size ground collider silently blocked shots at things below y = 0.'],\n  ['What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?', 'The Intent layer with the shared Bot and the story stage system. Everything else, from attract mode to the playthrough test, hangs off them. After that, the over-the-shoulder aiming with hit zones built from joint positions.'],\n  ['What was the hardest part about using the engine?', 'Working out frame and input timing at low frame rates in the software WebGPU browser here: which presses survive, when a level swap really happens, and what can run at time scale 0.'],\n  ['What did you change in the engine, and why? (none if nothing)', 'none'],\n  ['If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?', 'Let gamepad presses reach wasPressed at time scale 0, the way keyboard presses do, so a frozen menu needs no separate pad reading. An official shoulder-offset third-person rig would also save replacing rig.step by hand.'],\n];\nexport const PROMPT_FEEDBACK = [\n  ['What did you like most about this prompt?', 'The plan is a complete design with verified engine facts, real numbers and a real script. I could spend the effort on building instead of guessing. The originality guardrails were clear too.'],\n  ['What was confusing?', 'Mostly the Online line, which is only a link, until the plan explained it. The plan also lists more animations and props than a single vertical slice strictly needs, so I had to judge where a shared clip was good enough.'],\n  ['What was the hardest thing to do?', 'Keeping every system working together across a long linear game alone: the Dame, the crowd AI, checkpoints and set pieces all interact, and most of the serious bugs were at those joins. I could not judge game feel with hands on a pad here, only through the bot and screenshots.'],\n  ['What would you change in this prompt?', 'Ask for a short human-style feel checklist that a script can approximate, and say up front which listed assets are required and which are optional. A real person should still play it: balance here was only tuned against the bot.'],\n];\n\"\"\"\ns=s[:a]+new+s[b:]\ns=s.replace(\"testing: 'Headless node scripts and Playwright browsers on this computer, behind one command; stand-ins for pad, touch, audio and second player; no subagents for review'\",\"testing: 'Headless node scripts and Playwright browsers on this computer, behind one command (node tools/test.mjs): a scripted whole-game playthrough, unit and AI suites, stubbed gamepad, phone profile, Web Audio levels, two-page parties, the AI Hub harness. No subagents for review. No human playtest.'\")\ns=s.replace(\"research: 'Read the design plan, the engine kit guide, API and assets docs, and the AI Hub protocol README. No web research on the source.'\",\"research: 'Read the design plan, the engine kit guide, API and assets docs, and the AI Hub protocol README and example. No web research on the source.'\")\ns=s.replace(\"audio: 'All code. Song data for ten original pieces at 10 percent music by default, about 60 synthesised sound effects, Animalese-style gibberish voices per speaker'\",\"audio: 'All code, no files. Ten original songs as data with music at 10 percent by default, about 60 synthesised sound effects, Animalese-style gibberish voices per speaker'\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nP\ngrep -n \"—\\|–\" src/data/about.js | cut -c1-80; grep -n \"\\\"\" src/data/about.js | grep -v \"^.*export\" | head -3 | cut -c1-80\n(timeout 590 node tools/test.mjs 2>&1 | cut -c1-400 | tail -14)","description":"Fill feedback answers, then run the complete test suite","timeout":598000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1988,"cache_read_input_tokens":742460,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1988},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76d12802-c986-437e-adae-1ae347966275","uuid":"184ef51e-e723-4dec-81a7-015ed814a87b","timestamp":"2026-11-06T00:59:49.242Z","request_id":"req_011CgkmXoAbuko9PgbBuwWTS","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01XkEmEnyjCVYboWjvsS5LC5":{"command":"python3 - <<'P'\np='src/game/launch.js';s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"P.noMove = true; this.run.health =\",\"P.noMove = true; this.infiniteAmmo = true; this.run.health =\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='src/data/about.js';s=open(p).read()\nimport re\na=s.index(\"export const TESTING_FEEDBACK\"); b=s.index(\"export const CREDITS\")\nnew = r\"\"\"export const TESTING_FEEDBACK = [\n  ['How many issues did testing catch?', 'About 35 real issues: roughly 20 from the whole-game bot playthrough, 3 from the node suites, 12 from browser and harness runs. Many more were bugs in the bot or the tests themselves, which I do not count.'],\n  ['How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?', 'About 12. Reloading a checkpoint lost the nested story script and left the game stuck. Set pieces changed shared level data, which broke every retry. A checkpoint taken mid-vault put you inside a wall. Gate opening crashed. The road had no door action, so no way forward. The final boss valves could not be hit. Launch mines sat under the ground collider. Opening the Case with Triangle dropped your gun. Esc and I opened a menu