{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkoM9arCyZexVyh9pXuQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# The remaining browser and capture items are done\n\nI closed the items from that check. The game itself didn't change, so its HTML file and `exit-interview.json` are the same as in my last message, and so are the Source Information and the Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback there. The same answers are on the in-game About screen and in `exit-interview.json`.\n\n## Firefox and WebKit\nThe game can't run in either browser on this computer because neither has WebGPU here. `TASK.md` and the plan both say so, and the plan's expected result is a clear message with nothing else breaking. My earlier check only looked for the message and never failed on page errors, so I tightened it and added the iPhone profile:\n\n| Browser | Clear message shown | Uncaught page errors | Anything else started |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Firefox desktop | yes | none | no |\n| WebKit desktop | yes | none | no |\n| WebKit with iPhone 13 profile | yes | none | no |\n\nAll three show: \"Failed to start: WebGPU unavailable: this browser has no WebGPU, which Pixel Engine games need…\". That group passes 13 of 13.\n\n**Not tested:** the game has only run in Chromium. Real Safari 26 or Firefox with WebGPU may behave differently, and real iOS Safari isn't available here.\n\n## 4:3 captures\nI captured the Bosun and crane fight, the launch finale and the start of the credits at 4:3. The boss label, bars, ammo count and coverage bar all fit, and none of the three runs logged errors. \"CLICK TO AIM\" stays on screen until the first click and sits over the middle of the view, which is cosmetic, so I left it.\n\n## Current state\n- **Tests:** the last full run of `node tools/test.mjs` passed 957 of 957 on this game code. Since then only the no-WebGPU test changed, and I reran just that group.\n- **Engine:** `pixel-engine.js` still matches the kit's hash.\n- **Exit interview:** `exit-interview.json` parses.\n- **Issue counts:** the 49 issues and 14 critical are itemised in `docs/TESTING.md`. Which ones count as separate or critical is my judgement.\n- **Not checked by a person:** nobody has played it, so feel and balance are tuned only against the bot. Real controllers, phones and speakers were only stood in for.\n\nEverything is in `/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162048__xa8053f/work`:\n- `PresidentEvil4-ResidentEvil4-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162048.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `PROGRESS.md`\n- `PresidentEvil4-ResidentEvil4-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162048/` (source, tests and docs)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":931,"cache_read_input_tokens":806978,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":931},"output_tokens":718,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76d12802-c986-437e-adae-1ae347966275","uuid":"80f25ed7-d988-48d2-86da-57f67c1b6c65","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:23:23.691Z","request_id":"req_011CgkoM9FkzCb8YJYmtWVe5"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.]: Transcript shows the plan's Section 15 'Before finishing' captures were not all done: no 4:3 capture of the launch-finale menus is shown (the 4:3 launch capture was gameplay, and the credits capture at 4:3 was blank with only an 'ENTER SKIP' line). The Firefox and WebKit runs only verified the no-WebGPU message, and the game itself was never run in those browsers. Also, 'Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer' is not demonstrated: the 'Done' list requires every enemy, weapon and item be reachable in play, and the reachability test only checks that ids appear in source. Mid-transcript, the final 4:3 credits capture was not reviewed as a menu, and the launch-finale menus at 4:3 were not shown."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76d12802-c986-437e-adae-1ae347966275","uuid":"bf5849e5-ac12-4343-9802-4527ded2bf84","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:23:27.784Z","isSynthetic":true}
