{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgkq39aqmD1FTSJAhdcgP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Firefox and WebKit: tested, and the game can't run in them on this computer\n\nLast time I said this couldn't be done based only on `TASK.md`. I've now tested it directly, and no further work here can change the result:\n\n| Browser | WebGPU result | Game starts? | What the player sees | Page errors |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Firefox, default | `navigator.gpu` missing | No | Clear \"WebGPU unavailable\" message | None |\n| Firefox, WebGPU forced on | `requestAdapter()` returns no adapter | No | Same message | None |\n| WebKit | `navigator.gpu` missing | No | Same message | None |\n\nThe engine renders only through WebGPU, and `TASK.md` requires it to stay as shipped, so these browsers have nothing to run the game on. The only way to make it run would be swapping the renderer, which that rule forbids.\n\nThis also meets the plan. Section 15 says: \"WebKit and Firefox here have no WebGPU: expect the engine's clear message, and check that it appears and nothing else breaks.\" The message appears and nothing else breaks. The probe is saved as `tests/browser/nogpu_probe.py`; it isn't part of the main suite and only reports what it finds. The suite has its own check for the message and page errors.\n\n## Where things stand\n- **Tests:** 1016 of 1016 on the final code, with the game running in Chromium on WebGPU. Nothing in the game has changed since that run.\n- **Handed in:** the game's HTML file, `exit-interview.json` and the dev folder are all in place. The Source Information and all three feedback sections are on the About screen and in `exit-interview.json`, with the latest counts: 50 issues, 14 critical.\n- **Only a person or other hardware can check:**\n    - how the game feels and how well it's balanced;\n    - real controllers, phones, speakers and TVs;\n    - Firefox or Safari on a machine with working WebGPU.\n\nI don't have anything further to do on this computer for this goal. If the stop check still objects to Firefox and WebKit, the only way forward is a machine where those browsers have WebGPU. I won't report them as passing a game run that can't happen here."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":750,"cache_read_input_tokens":827648,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":750},"output_tokens":701,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76d12802-c986-437e-adae-1ae347966275","uuid":"85304100-f96c-4f69-b24d-9e474f5be8a9","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:45:30.304Z","request_id":"req_011Cgkq39FFPT9EG6n4PaXtX"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.]: Not satisfied. The last assistant message says it cannot verify the game in Firefox or WebKit and that real-browser play is untested. The plan's Section 15 asks for the engine's clear message and that nothing else breaks, which was checked, but the Done list requires everything that can be done on this computer, and 'Firefox or Safari on a machine with working WebGPU' is left undone. The message also says the game was 'tested' there, which the evidence does not support: the probe only checked for the no-WebGPU message on Firefox and WebKit. Playing the game in those browsers was not attempted with any available means."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76d12802-c986-437e-adae-1ae347966275","uuid":"b1af7b16-e91c-4d0a-889e-3d31c1273ead","timestamp":"2026-11-06T01:45:34.184Z","isSynthetic":true}
