{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkrttKpZizf3rNPYQ4s1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# President Evil 4 now runs in Firefox too\n\nThe full suite passes **1091 of 1091** on the final code, and that now includes the game itself running in Firefox. Everything `TASK.md` asks for is in this folder.\n\n## Correction: I was wrong about Firefox\nI told you twice the game couldn't run in Firefox on this computer. It can. My first attempt failed only because it had no display. With WebGPU forced on and a virtual display, Firefox gets an adapter and the game runs.\n\n| Browser | Result |\n|---|---|\n| **Chromium** | Everything in the suite passes |\n| **Firefox** | Passes boot and audio, pad, keyboard and mouse, menus, attract mode, solo Night Shift, same-computer parties and WebRTC invite codes. I also looked at a captured siege frame, which looks the same as in Chromium |\n| **WebKit** | Shows the clear \"WebGPU unavailable\" message with no page errors. It has no `navigator.gpu` even when launched directly with its WebGPU feature on, so there's nothing to run the game on |\n\n**Firefox caveats:**\n- **Settings:** WebGPU had to be forced on with preferences and a virtual display, so an ordinary Firefox on Linux would still show the message.\n- **Sound:** Firefox has no sound output here, and even a plain test page fails the same way. I gave it a private silent audio device, stopped afterwards, and measured the music level there; nobody heard it.\n- **Scope:** the AI Hub harness and the phone test ran only in Chromium, and only the Chromium build had the full capture review.\n\n## Failures on the way to the final run\n- **False failure in Firefox:** the music check failed once in the full suite after passing by hand. My test setup was at fault: this folder's path is too long for a Unix socket, so the audio server left a stray `PresidentEvil` socket file that blocked later runs. I removed it and switched to TCP on an OS-picked 127.0.0.1 port. The check then passed three times in a row and again in the final run.\n- **Earlier browser crash:** one earlier crash never had a confirmed cause, because I lost the traceback. I closed the likely race, and it hasn't come back.\n\n## What only a person or other hardware can check\n- How the game feels and how well it's balanced; nobody has played it, and it was tuned only against the bot.\n- Real controllers, phones, speakers and TVs, which were only stood in for.\n- Real Safari or iOS, and Firefox with WebGPU on by default.\n\n## Source Information and feedback\nThese stand as in my earlier message, with these updates:\n- **Testing:** the game also ran in Firefox with WebGPU forced on, a virtual display and a silent audio device.\n- **Testing Feedback:** 50 issues, 14 critical, itemised in `docs/TESTING.md`.\n- **Engine Feedback:** two wrong guesses are now on record, the pad presses at time scale 0 and Firefox being unable to run the game.\n\nThe current text is on the About screen and in `exit-interview.json`, and the engine's hash still matches the kit's. To rerun the suite, first run `npm install` in the dev folder. The Firefox part also needs `xvfb-run` and `pulseaudio`, which are on this computer.\n\nEverything is in `/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162048__xa8053f/work`:\n- `PresidentEvil4-ResidentEvil4-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162048.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `PROGRESS.md`\n- `PresidentEvil4-ResidentEvil4-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162048/`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":246,"cache_read_input_tokens":860567,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":246},"output_tokens":703,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76d12802-c986-437e-adae-1ae347966275","uuid":"7dbbfa8c-bc67-4c03-97dc-b8100ed5bf96","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:09:55.550Z","request_id":"req_011CgkrtszEyA2JZ6LDYMB4t"}
