{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgktfxcfjDMi6AAGLafZA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# President Evil 4 is finished: 1100 of 1100 tests pass\n\nEverything in `PLAN.md` that can be done on this computer is done, and everything `TASK.md` asks for is in this folder. Those 1100 checks all ran on the final code in a single run of `node tools/test.mjs`, covering Chromium and Firefox.\n\n## What this last round added\n- **AI Hub harness in Firefox:** all four scenarios now run there as well as in Chromium.\n- **Touch-only behaviour in Firefox:** this passes, but Playwright's Firefox can't pretend to be a touch device, so I stubbed what the game's detection reads. Real touch hardware is still untested.\n- **Area captures in Firefox:** I checked frames from six areas (cannery, yard, causeway, abbey, nave, launch) on top of the earlier siege frame, and they render correctly.\n- **A real bug the repeat runs caught:** if the host left just after a round started on a slow machine, the hub's traffic check could fail, and the hub keeps out any game that fails it. Copies now say hello as soon as they're ready and start sending from the start event. Host-leave then passed six times in a row under the same heavy load, and again in the final run.\n- **Test runner fix:** it was undercounting Firefox results and hiding failure details; both are fixed.\n\n## Browser results\n\n| Browser | Result |\n|---|---|\n| **Chromium** | Everything passes |\n| **Firefox** | The game, parties, AI Hub harness and touch-only flow pass; needs WebGPU forced on, a virtual display and a silent audio device |\n| **WebKit** | Shows the clear \"WebGPU unavailable\" message with no page errors; it has no `navigator.gpu` even launched directly with its feature on, so the game can't run there |\n\n## What this computer can't check\n- How the game feels and whether it's balanced: nobody has played it, and it was tuned only against the bot.\n- Real controllers, touch devices, speakers and TVs, which were only stood in for.\n- Real Safari or iOS, and Firefox with WebGPU on by default.\n\n## Source Information and feedback\nThese stand as in my earlier full message, with these updates:\n- **Testing:** the game, the AI Hub harness and a stubbed touch-only device also ran in Firefox with WebGPU forced on.\n- **Testing Feedback:** 51 issues, 15 critical, itemised in `docs/TESTING.md`: 21 from the bot playthrough, 8 from Node suites, 11 from browser and harness runs, 10 from captures, 1 from checking the code against the plan. Bugs in the bot or tests aren't counted, and how to split them or which count as critical is my judgement.\n- **Engine Feedback:** two wrong guesses are on record: dropped pad presses at time scale 0, and Firefox being unable to run the game.\n\nThe current text is on the About screen and in `exit-interview.json`, which parses, and the engine's hash still matches the kit's.\n\nTo rerun the suite, first run `npm install` in the dev folder. The Firefox part also needs `xvfb-run` and `pulseaudio`, which are on this computer.\n\nEverything is in `/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162048__xa8053f/work`:\n- `PresidentEvil4-ResidentEvil4-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162048.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `PROGRESS.md`\n- `PresidentEvil4-ResidentEvil4-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-162048/`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":458,"cache_read_input_tokens":877362,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":458},"output_tokens":706,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76d12802-c986-437e-adae-1ae347966275","uuid":"99f0d2c3-a8ad-4b9f-8947-2bf1e2815a11","timestamp":"2026-11-06