{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MXrM1KQ9Msmkv6KT1nsQBX","type":"tool_result","content":"48 passed, 0 failed\n5:**Node (`Engine.headless`, fast **[verified: 120 frames with 7 puppets in under a second, replay equal, join\n6:- Maps: paint, every cell reachable, markers exist. Case: fit, rotate, arrange, overflow, combine. Shop: buy\n7:- AI: tokens never exceeded; a crowd of 30 reaches a player and attacks; door bash; vault; ladder; floor lin\n8:- Set pieces: Winch reaches 100%; crane drop stuns the Bosun; lens puzzle; tide kills on time; QTE success a\n9:- **The whole game, played by a bot (`src/game/bot.js`):** each area's data has a plan (`goto`, `kill`, `int\n10:- Replay: record 60 s of a siege with `engine.recording()`, replay, compare `fingerprint()`.\n11:- Attract: idle title 600 frames starts it; any key or pad press exits; it loops through all clips with no \n12:- Co-op sim: host and client game objects through a fake `session` with latency: snapshots stay under 1,200\n14:**Browser (deliverable from `file://`, unless the harness):**\n15:- Boots with no console errors; `engine.errors` and `gpuErrors` empty; the kit's own `node check.mjs` passe\n16:- Gamepad stub (`add_init_script` replacing `navigator.getGamepads` with a standard-mapping pad): menus, ai\n17:- Phone profile (Chromium, touch): touch controls absent, required panel shown, attract running, tap doesn'\n18:- Audio: first boot `audio.volume.music === 0.1`; music bus `AnalyserNode` level above silence; Reset retur\n19:- Dev mode reachable from pause; slider changes `TUNING` live; reset restores.\n20:- About screen has all pages; exit interview parses.\n21:- **Hub harness:** the harness only loads same-origin pages and imports `./bridge.js` and `./round.js`, so \n22:- Standalone: outside a session the deliverable runs normally. Two pages in one context run a Night Shift p\n23:- WebKit and Firefox here have no WebGPU: expect the engine's clear message, and check that it appears and \n### What this computer doesn't have\n\nNo script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here\n\n- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init\n- **No touch device.** Use Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, which have touch, and tap with page.touchscreen.\n- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\n- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\n- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\n- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\n\n### Sharing this computer","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76d12802-c986-437e-adae-1ae347966275","uuid":"5aee62f5-56bf-45c6-b9a2-c5f97c52c170","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:43:24.925Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"48 passed, 0 failed\n5:**Node (`Engine.headless`, fast **[verified: 120 frames with 7 puppets in under a second, replay equal, join\n6:- Maps: paint, every cell reachable, markers exist. Case: fit, rotate, arrange, overflow, combine. Shop: buy\n7:- AI: tokens never exceeded; a crowd of 30 reaches a player and attacks; door bash; vault; ladder; floor lin\n8:- Set pieces: Winch reaches 100%; crane drop stuns the Bosun; lens puzzle; tide kills on time; QTE success a\n9:- **The whole game, played by a bot (`src/game/bot.js`):** each area's data has a plan (`goto`, `kill`, `int\n10:- Replay: record 60 s of a siege with `engine.recording()`, replay, compare `fingerprint()`.\n11:- Attract: idle title 600 frames starts it; any key or pad press exits; it loops through all clips with no \n12:- Co-op sim: host and client game objects through a fake `session` with latency: snapshots stay under 1,200\n14:**Browser (deliverable from `file://`, unless the harness):**\n15:- Boots with no console errors; `engine.errors` and `gpuErrors` empty; the kit's own `node check.mjs` passe\n16:- Gamepad stub (`add_init_script` replacing `navigator.getGamepads` with a standard-mapping pad): menus, ai\n17:- Phone profile (Chromium, touch): touch controls absent, required panel shown, attract running, tap doesn'\n18:- Audio: first boot `audio.volume.music === 0.1`; music bus `AnalyserNode` level above silence; Reset retur\n19:- Dev mode reachable from pause; slider changes `TUNING` live; reset restores.\n20:- About screen has all pages; exit interview parses.\n21:- **Hub harness:** the harness only loads same-origin pages and imports `./bridge.js` and `./round.js`, so \n22:- Standalone: outside a session the deliverable runs normally. Two pages in one context run a Night Shift p\n23:- WebKit and Firefox here have no WebGPU: expect the engine's clear message, and check that it appears and \n### What this computer doesn't have\n\nNo script can check these, so they're written by hand. Test with the stand-ins; anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here\n\n- **No physical controller.** Emulate one: replace navigator.getGamepads with a stub that returns a pad in the standard mapping (Playwright's add_init\n- **No touch device.** Use Playwright's phone and tablet profiles, which have touch, and tap with page.touchscreen.\n- **Nobody to listen.** Check sound by what Web Audio produces: render it with an OfflineAudioContext, or read levels from an AnalyserNode.\n- **No second player.** Play multiplayer with two browser pages (or contexts) on this computer.\n- **No real iPhone or iPad.** WebKit with an iPhone profile is the closest; it isn't iOS Safari.\n- **No TV.** Judge the 10-foot view from screenshots at 1920×1080.\n\n### Sharing this computer","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_res