{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkvFVybAf28ki942fZGR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This objection raises nothing new that I can act on, so I'm not doing more work or running the tests again for the sake of another pass.\n\n- **Human play:** this can't be done here, because no person is on this computer. Reachability was shown by the bot run and the area sweep.\n- **Real hardware:** `TASK.md` says this computer has none, and that anything needing it is \"never required\". I used the stand-ins it names.\n- **WebKit:** the game can't run there. WebKit has no `navigator.gpu` here, even launched directly with its feature on, and the engine needs WebGPU and has to stay as shipped. The plan's §15 expects the clear message for this case, and that passes.\n- **Firefox:** forcing WebGPU on with a virtual display is the only way it runs here. With those, the game, the AI Hub harness and parties all pass.\n- **Order of the printouts:** `STAGE.md` and the Done list were printed later than they could have been, but all the work and the checks against them came before the final 1163 of 1163 run. Printing them earlier wouldn't change any result.\n\nBy the goal's own wording, \"can be done on this computer\", I consider this done. The remaining items need a person or other hardware, and I won't describe them as checked.\n\nThe stop check may keep objecting on these same points, since it seems to want evidence this machine can't produce. If so, you can end it with `/goal clear`. If you'd rather have something specific done, such as a Safari check on your machine or tuning after you've played it, tell me and I'll pick it up."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1039,"cache_read_input_tokens":915687,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1039},"output_tokens":5,"service_tie