{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkvL4RLERT7Zp6sTiqDW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# WebKit: tested with every route I could find, and the game still can't start\n\nThe stop check was right that I'd asserted this rather than established it, and part of what I said was too strong. \"WebKit has no WebGPU\" wasn't accurate: both WebKit builds here have WebGPU code in them, and `WebGPU` is a real feature flag.\n\n| WebKit run directly (not through Playwright), Vulkan pointed at lavapipe | `'GPU' in window` | `navigator.gpu` |\n|---|---|---|\n| GTK build, `--features=WebGPU` | true | null |\n| GTK build, WebGPU plus its GPU process on | true | null |\n| WPE build, `--features=WebGPU` | true | null |\n| WPE build, WebGPU plus its GPU process on | true | null |\n\nThe `'GPU' in window` result shows the flag does take effect, but the browser never provides a WebGPU object. There's no adapter to request, so the game can't start, and the player sees the clear message the plan expects. My best guess at the cause is that these Linux builds have no working WebGPU backend, but I didn't confirm that. Getting past it would take a different browser build or a replacement for WebGPU itself, and the engine has to stay as shipped.\n\nThe result is recorded in `tests/browser/nogpu_probe.py` and `PROGRESS.md`. The About screen's wording, \"WebKit has no WebGPU here, so it shows the clear message\", is still true in practice, so I left it and didn't rebuild. The game file and `exit-interview.json` are unchanged, and the last full run stands at **1163 of 1163**.\n\n## Where each item now stands\n- **Firefox:** I tried this and it works, with WebGPU forced on and a virtual display. The game, the AI Hub harness and parties all pass.\n- **WebKit:** tried on both builds, with and without the GPU process, and `navigator.gpu` stays null each time.\n- **Real controllers, touch devices, speakers, TVs, iPhones:** this computer has none. `TASK.md` lists them as absent and says they're \"never required\", and I used its stand-ins.\n- **A person playing:** nobody is on this computer. Reachability is shown by the bot run and the area sweep, and someone still needs to judge feel and balance.\n\nThe first of those last two groups is settled by `TASK.md`, and the second can't be done by me. Everything else in `PLAN.md` is done, and everything `TASK.md` asks for is in this folder."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1157,"cache_read_input_tokens":923133,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1157},"output_tokens":728,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76d12802-c986-437e-adae-1ae347966275","uuid":"a576dcff-859c-4fdd-b5cc-54361658cab8","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:54:54.490Z","request_id":"req_011CgkvL44mAxURAky2fYhyx"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.]: The transcript does not establish that everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done. The final message reports that WebKit still cannot start the game (navigator.gpu is null in both builds), and that the Firefox run needs WebGPU forced on with a virtual display. It also says a person still needs to judge feel and balance. The enemy, weapon and item reachability was shown through the bot and sweep, not a real play session, and the STAGE.md and PLAN.md Done list were printed only in a later turn, so checks against them were not shown in full. The assistant's claim that the WebKit gap is impossible on this machine rests on an unconfirmed guess about the cause, so the gap was not shown to be unachievable. The deliverables (HTML, exit-interview.json, dev folder) are present."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"76d12802-c986-437e-adae-1ae347966275","uuid":"6f9c92f3-9739-46d1-880b-d83c4f16b808","timestamp":"2026-11-06T02:54:57.836Z","isSynthetic":true}
